    decision the VICTIM receives the native killp relay (v527f5 mechanism): their
    own client executes the pilot death at the live moment - real death flow,
    real respawn - and its later report is absorbed by the swallow guard. Peers
    keep the immediate 0x55+hunter canopy delete (= the killer's live cyan).
    VERIFIED: no world teardown, correct cyan, single scoring.
    NEXT (open): cockpit-kill killer-side cyan. Two-gate model PROVEN from
    messages21: (1) third-party viewers draw iff ExitDataArrive resolves the
    victim to a PILOT NAME (player-bound; lazily-created object-only peers show
    a plane-type string and draw nothing); (2) the KILLER's own client also
    needs the 2009 killer-directed 14-byte msg-33 (seen in the 2009 capture
    messages04 as 'in 33'14') - without it, name-bound synthesised kills draw
    nothing for the killer (cockpit kill 20:41:48 run_20260830_200618). Plan:
    RE FUN_004f9b0f's 14B payload layout, then send a populated TYPE-0x53
    msg-33 to the killer on every synthesised kill; watch for double HUD credit.
v527f5 [NATIVE MODERATOR RELAY] - killp/ejectp/crumblep now FORWARD the action
    to the TARGET's client ([7f][target player_index u16][sub], appspace T=0x42,
    the exact shape the client emits as 'out 127'4') and send nothing else: the
    target's FA.exe executes its own death natively and its report drives the
    normal kill chain. Replaces the server-side delete of the target's own
    object, which tore the victim's world down (a client NEVER receives an
    outside delete of its own live object in normal play). ##killp self-test:
    "All worked as expected for the first time". crumblep now draws the native
    "X has Exploded Y" cyan (MEC=6).
v526f5 - server chute-kill broadcast is peers-only for good (owner-inclusion
