v519f5/v520f5 [SERVER-AUTHORITATIVE CHUTE KILL - THE 2009 ARCHITECTURE] - the
    host, not the victim's client, decides the pilot kill: count the relayed
    msg-29 hit records per canopy; at PARA_KILL_HITS (3) broadcast the native
    0x55+hunter canopy delete to peers at the live moment (+50 killer score,
    victim pilot-loss). Root insight: the victim's client defers its chute-death
    report until RESPAWN (flightrec-proven: the delete arrives bundled with the
    StartPlace request), so victim-driven kills can never be live; the canopy
    has no telemetry and the client waits for the server to end it - the server
