v508f5 [RESUPPLY - REPAIR REQUIRES ENGINE-OFF] The client sends msg-119 ONLY with
      the engine off (user-confirmed), so the server tracks it: a 119 latches
      s._engine_off=True; ANY movement clears it (poll re-arm). The poll's damaged-
      repair trigger (v506f5) now requires _engine_off, so a plane on the ground with
      the engine ON is NOT auto-repaired even under fire - the pilot must cut the
      engine (fires a fresh 119) to ask for service. USER-VERIFIED. Edge (noted, not
      fixed): engine off->on while perfectly braked (no movement, no message) still
      reads engine-off to the server; closing it needs the engine-toggle message
      mapped (RE task).
v507f5 [RESUPPLY - NO REPAIR WHILE UNDER FIRE] A damaged plane waits until incoming
      fire has stopped for REPAIR_UNDER_FIRE_HOLDOFF_S (5.0s, from last_damaged_at)
      before it repairs, so a parked plane can't out-repair a sustained strafing run
      (each repair also clears the attacker's held kill). Enforced in the poll (holds
      off, one-shot NOT set, services the instant the hold-off elapses) and the
      explicit 119 (defers to the poll). Non-damaged loadout grants unaffected. 0
      disables. USER-VERIFIED.
v506f5 [RESUPPLY - PARKED-AND-HIT REPAIR] A plane already parked engine-off when hit
      never fires a fresh 119 (no engine-off transition), so nothing requested the
      repair and it sat damaged until the pilot toggled the engine
      (run_20260830_032805). Fix: a new hit (msg-28) re-arms the resupply one-shot,
      and the poll honors took_damage as a repair trigger (like a pending 119) even
      in an air-start arena. [v508f5 later gated this on engine-off.] USER-VERIFIED.
v505f5 [RESUPPLY - DEFERRED-119 RETRY IN AIR-START ARENAS] Root of the online 'repair
      only after an engine toggle': the FFA arena is AIR-START (StartGround=no), which
      SUPPRESSES the background poll grant, so the explicit 119 was the ONLY repair
      path - and a deferred 119 (plane not settled that instant) had NOTHING to retry
      it (the client fires 119 once and drops it). Now a deferred 119 is remembered
      (s._repair_119_pending) and the 0.5s poll services it the instant the plane
      settles, honored with explicit=True to bypass the air-start suppression.
      REPAIR_119_PENDING_WINDOW_S=10s. USER-VERIFIED (defer -> poll-service handoff).
v504f5 [RESUPPLY - SETTLE GATE JUDGES RECENT MOTION] ground_stop_eligible required
      plane_movement()==0 over the FULL CRASH_MOVEMENT_WINDOW_S (3s), so a plane that
      had just rolled to a stop kept non-zero movement (the roll-out lingering in the
      3s history, e.g. movement=25729) and false-negatived as 'not settled' for ~3s
      after it was actually still (online run_181723: granted at 0, DEFERRED at
      25729). New plane_movement_recent(s, GROUND_STOP_MOVE_LOOKBACK_S=1.0) judges
      only the last ~1s; the full-window plane_movement is UNTOUCHED for the crash
      classifier (deaths unchanged), and the poll's movement= re-arm still fires for a
      flying plane. USER-VERIFIED (landing repair, small tunable delay).
v503f5 [NETWORK/CTD - LOBBY-EXIT-AFTER-BAIL CTD: THE ROOT FIX] Bail -> exit to HQ
      under canopy -> back to lobby CTD'd the client every time ('generic error,
      Length=-8/-11, Network.cpp:249'; messages87/89/91) while exit-to-desktop was
      clean. Root: the msg-3 router runs `(entered_game or _left_world) and
      sub==0x03`. A normal exit brings the plane down IN-ARENA, which sets
      _left_world, so the teardown's trailing deletes are swallowed. After a BAIL
      the plane is still airborne at the leave - its ExitEvent fires INSIDE the
      client's ~GAME_DEF, arriving with entered_game=False (msg-64 cleared it)
      AND _left_world=False -> router miss -> DEFAULT ECHO -> the client
      re-ingests its own 'out 3'4' mid-teardown ('in 3'4 / Server require delete
      object N', N garbage 0/1/120) -> negative-length CTD. Desktop exits closed
      the socket before the echo landed, which is why only the lobby path died.
      Fix: s._left_world = True at the top of the msg-64 leave handler - every
      post-leave msg-3 now routes to the guarded swallow, however the life ended.
      Fresh spawn re-arms it. USER-VERIFIED clean. (v501f5/v502f5 below were
      chased first and stay in as correct behavior, but the echo was a FRESH
      post-leave send neither could touch.)
v502f5 [NETWORK - STALE IN-GAME RELIABLE STOP ON LEAVE] Defence layer found while
      chasing the CTD: the un-ACKed reliable backlog (RELBUDGET 32-56 at a
      bail-leave) kept being retransmitted into the client's ~GAME_DEF by BOTH
      the send_rel blocking window and _rel_keeper. New s._arena_left_at stamp at
      the msg-64 leave; both retransmit loops now drop any packet whose window
      predates the stamp ('arena left - stale in-game reliable dropped').
      Post-leave lobby sends have a later t0 and are untouched. Not the CTD root
      (the crash was an echo, a fresh send) but stops a real hazard class -
      kept. A DESKTOP exit never needed it (s.closing already stops the keeper).
v501f5 [SCORE/CTD - BAIL-EXIT HUSK DESPAWN (the v370f5 'quits mid-descent' gap)]
      A bailer who exits to HQ while still under canopy left the empty bail
      plane flying with nothing to tear it down - the exact STILL-OPEN route the
      credit_bail_husk_kill docstring documented (husk orphaned on peers, held
      bail kill lost). Now: when the parachuter is removed with exit-to-HQ
      (MEC nibble 10) and bailed_plane_obj is live, despawn the husk RIGHT THEN
      (broadcast_object_delete_3, peers only) and consume the held kill through
      the same credit_bail_husk_kill path the respawn-despawn uses; then CLEAR
      my_obj_number so the leave cannot re-delete a plane that is already gone.
      v501f5.1: the first cut never fired - the `_bp2 != my_obj_number` guard was
      copied from the respawn path where they differ, but at exit-to-HQ there is
      no respawn so they are EQUAL; guard dropped (run_192959 proved the miss).
      Flag: BAIL_EXIT_HUSK_DESPAWN. Verified firing (run_195611).
v500f5 [RESUPPLY - 2009 SERVICE DELAY: EXPLICIT 119 GATED ON GROUND-STOP SETTLE]
      USER-VERIFIED ("worked well", settle raised 2.0 -> 3.0s). The explicit
      msg-119 repair request was serviced the instant it arrived - even
      mid-landing-rollout (run_183819: grants at movement=261238/249897) - while
      the background poll already waited AUTO_RESUPPLY_SETTLE. The 2009 host
      made you sit ~2s before service. Fix: the 119 now requires the SAME
      ground_stop_eligible settle as the poll (flag SERVICE_REQUIRES_GROUND_STOP;
      not-settled requests log 'msg-119 request DEFERRED' - client re-asks, poll
      is the fallback). Accepted trade: partially re-opens the v454f5
      grant-on-request rationale; watch for a genuinely parked plane deferring.
      KNOWN OPEN (separate): a parked BOMBER's 119 is refused by the v446f5
      bombsight/special-form guard ('special telemetry form seen 0.1s ago') -
      the bombsight runs on the ground, so bombers cannot repair at all. Needs a
      parked-vs-bombrun discriminator; not attempted (delicate).
v499f5 [RESUPPLY - REVERTED SAME DAY: PEER-REFRESH DELAY WAS THE WRONG LAYER]
      First cut at the 2009 delay put a debounced threading.Timer on the v495f5
      REPAIR-VIS peer re-create. Wrong layer twice over: it only delays what the
      OBSERVER sees (needs took_damage, i.e. player-inflicted damage - solo tests
      can never trigger it), and the thing the user was timing was the service
      grant itself. Cleanly reverted (constant + delayed block removed); the
      correct fix is v500f5.
v498f5 [SCORE - PILOT-FATE FIX PAIR: ON-CHUTE BAIL + PRE-GUARD PARACHUTER HOIST]
      (1) An empty bail plane comes down MEC=1, not 5, and was booked as a
      cockpit death - new _on_chute first-branch defers the fate to the canopy.
      (2) THE capture bug: the parachuter-delete handler lived inside the
      `entered_game and not _left_world` guard, but the bail sets _left_world
      when the empty plane comes down, so the canopy's later SE=12 delete was
      swallowed and CAPTURED never scored (run_160000). Hoisted a pre-guard
      parachuter block ahead of the guard: read stored[7], SE=12 ->
      db_credit_capture + aces wipe + ACE88, relay the chute delete, clear the
      tracker, return. VERIFIED: full 4/4 matrix in run_163649 (enemy chute ->
      CAPTURED death+1; friendly bail / crash-lands -> pilot safe, plane only;
      cockpit crash -> death). PILOT_FATE_SCORING left ON per user.
v497f5 [SCORE - PILOT SAFE/CAPTURED: FATE BY WHERE THE PILOT LANDS] 13-edit
      feature behind PILOT_FATE_SCORING. Bail = +1 plane lost always; the PILOT
      is lost only where FA itself says so - the parachuter's delete exit byte
      ((MEC<<4)|ScoreEvent at stored[7]): SE=12 (0x2c) = came down on enemy
      ground = CAPTURED (death +1, aces wiped, streak broken via new
      db_credit_capture); SE=0 (0x20) = friendly = safe (aces/streak kept).
      Crash-lands are always survivable - FA.exe FUN_00478640 computes the
      0xc-(territory-match) capture code for the PILOT/parachuter path only,
      proven behaviorally (same enemy field, bail=captured vs crash-land=safe,
      run_163649). Kill credit to the shooter is independent of pilot fate
      (db_credit_kill count_pilot_death param; score_on_death pilot_lost gate).
      Enemy crash-land=death was considered and DROPPED per user - TC territory
      flips at CapturePercent=50 make any server-side ownership map go stale.
v496f5 [NETWORK - CLOCK: STATUS KEEPER RUNS THROUGH LOBBY/HQ] Re-fix of the
      galloping-clock after the v493f5 revert, per the user's preferred
      direction: stop gating the 2s STATUS time-keeper on entered_game so the
      base credit never freezes during a lobby/HQ stay - no gap, no lump, no
      re-anchor needed under either clock model. STATUS: user says "looks ok,
      don't mark as fixed yet" - certification needs a long-idle re-fly with
      peers present (the v493f5 failure mode).
v495f5 [MULTIPLAYER - VISUAL REPAIR NOT SEEN BY PEERS: OBJECT RE-CREATE] Peers
      hold a damaged NetPlane's state until the object is (re)created - msg-88
      refreshes fuel/load only (v494f5 probe disproved it live). On a
      damaged->repaired transition the plane is now re-issued to every peer that
      has it, via the v474f5 ATOMIC predel+create (object-only,
      with_client=False). Broadcast PROVEN in the 2-pilot session (run_142512:
      're-created object on 2 peer(s)' on every repair). Behind
      REPAIR_REFRESH_PEERS. Known cosmetic: the re-create blips at (0,0,0)
      before telemetry snaps it back ('breaks in half'); fixing that means
      creating at the live position - open. The observer-delay question (2009
      showed damage for ~2s) is unresolved after the v499f5 revert - needs a
      shooter+target+observer pass to decide.
