v490f5 [NETWORK - TRANSPORT FIN-ACK: clean disconnect handshake (10s exit hang +
      dirty-close fix)] ROOT CAUSE of 'the game isn't really disconnecting correctly',
      found by RE of vcncNet.dll (loaded in Ghidra) + the client's own vcncnet logs:
      the close is TWO layers. (1) APP layer: vcncDisconnect sends the cmd=2 request
      (reliable, 4B pl=00000002) and requires a reply whose command field == 100
      (0x64) - v386f5's reply is CORRECT and the client consumes it. (2) TRANSPORT
      layer: the DLL then enters WaitForClose (FUN_10003e89), sends an 8-byte FIN
      control frame - [session-id u16 BE][flags u16 BE 0x0800 = type 4][dword 0] -
      and ONLY a received frame with the FIN flag (input dispatch FUN_100032da,
      state-4 branch -> FUN_10004170 -> 'Network connection closed.') ends the wait.
      We never sent one -> 'Resend FIN packet.' at +5s/+10s -> 10-SECOND HANG on
      EVERY exit -> forced dirty teardown ('~DLIS not empty, N elements remains' in
      every modern client log; the 2009 service closed properly - messages04 ends
      SUSPEND/RESUME + clean). Downstream of the dirty close: the client's clean-
      shutdown state-commit never runs -> the saved 'last aircraft + loadout' comes
      back STALE/out-of-order on reconnect (the wrong-aircraft reports; selection
      survives arena re-entries within a connection, scrambles across reconnects).
      * FIX: stateless FIN-ACK in the raw RX loop - an 8B datagram with wire byte2 ==
        0x08 (pure FIN) is answered by mirroring the client's id back with the FIN
        flag: data[:2] + 08 00 00 00 00 00. Stateless because the FIN arrives ~400ms
        after cmd=2 already tore the session down; idempotent per retransmit. Logged
        as FINACK. App-layer cmd=2/cmd=5 handling unchanged.
      * RE BONUS (banked): sending a FIN-flagged frame TO a connected client makes it
        FIN back twice and close cleanly (state-2 branch) = a graceful server-side
        KICK primitive for the future. Wire spec: flags u16 = (type<<9)|(size&0x1ff);
        types seen: 8=SYN, 4=FIN, 1=ACK-class; SYNACK id adopted from reply offset 10.
      VERIFY: vcncnet log shows 'Network connection closed.' (no Resend FIN) within
      ~1s of quitting; messagesXX ends with NO '~DLIS not empty'; then the real test -
      fly a plane, quit fully, reconnect: the SAME plane should be selected. Also
      expect faster relaunch loops (no 10s zombie socket).
      TESTED: transport close CONFIRMED CLEAN (vcncnet 20260827181347: FIN sent ->
      FIN-ACK received same millisecond -> 'Network connection closed!' -> no resends,
      ~2s total vs 10s). REMAINING: '~DLIS not empty' (3 elements) persists and the
      aircraft toggling persists -> the dirt is the APP/LOBBY layer, not transport.
      LOGIN-PHASE DIFF (2009 messages04 = bigalon's own live-service log, vs modern):
      the 2009 lobby answered RICH data where we send stubs - in 206'4949 (LARGE-
      chunked via in 1'1452 xN), 202'3350, 203'1374, 210'1110, 225'36 - and the
      client UPLOADS a 38-byte blob at login (out 228'38) that the 2009 server echoed
      back symmetric (in 228'38). That symmetric 228 exchange is the prime candidate
      for PERSONA persistence (hangar/last plane/loadout): within a connection the
      selection is in-memory; across connections the 2009 client got it FROM the
      server - we never send it -> stale/out-of-order local fallback = the toggling.
      * PROTO_WATCH gate change: entered_game condition REMOVED (login-time lobby 2xx
        now captured; pilot-name fallback to account/?). EXPERIMENT: two logins with
        different selected planes -> diff out-228 (and out-225) hex; if a byte tracks
        the plane -> implement store-per-account + echo-at-login (no field decode
        needed initially). SUSPEND/RESUME close choreography still banked (likely the
        ~DLIS cleanup); VCNCMD system-command numbers findable in vcncNet.dll SYSTEM
        dispatch when we take it up.

