v485f5 [MULTIPLAYER - PEER CREATE-BEFORE-TELEMETRY ORDER (CTD FIX) + DIAG] First
      2-player test on the GCP box CTD'd Bigalon the instant his client built the
      peer's NetPlane. Client (messages38): 'Get coord for missing object 256' ->
      create client 0 (Starfighter@FA) -> Create NetPlane (F4U-1c) -> Access
      violation 0x5F52454A type:1 (an EXECUTE fault through a vtable overwritten with
      ASCII 'JER_/_REJ'). Server (server__2_.log 20:07:20.576): CREATE2 client+object
      Starfighter St=0 ONumber=0x0100 plane=9 -> AC2E_Bigalon. ROOT CAUSE: the relay
      fires the create ASYNC (send pool, v357f5) but relays the sender's telemetry
      INLINE on the same frame, so telemetry BEAT the queued create; the peer stubbed
      the slot ('missing object N') and the first-create then landed on an occupied
      slot -> Network.cpp !Objects[N]/440 CTD. The v190 death-path comment ASSUMED
      'CREATE lands first, then telemetry', but the 'flying' filter only gates
      telemetry until ServerConfirm - it never actually ordered create vs telemetry.
      Record builders are FINE (build_client_record bounds the name, build_object_
      record lays St/ONumber/plane correctly) - it is purely ordering.
      * FIX: relay_telemetry now HOLDS a sender's telemetry to a peer until that
        peer's create has had time to arrive - skip the relay on the create-fire
        frame, then keep skipping until RELAY_CREATE_SETTLE_S (0.5s) has elapsed
        (_created_at[peer], refreshed on every (re)create; _created_peers pop at
        respawn re-arms it). Toggle RELAY_HOLD_TELEM_UNTIL_CREATE=False reverts to
        the old unordered behaviour. plane_movement/relay/tick paths untouched.
      * DIAG (CREATE-ORDER): logs 'create fired ... holding telemetry Ns' when the
        create goes out and 'telemetry released Nms after create (CREATE-first OK)'
        when it resumes - confirms the ordering per (sender->peer) pair on the next
        2-player run. Cost: the peer briefly holds the plane at the create position
        (0,0,0) until telemetry snaps it in - a short pop-in, not a crash.
      NOT the resupply chain, and NOT the 'Shadow' account (a SEPARATE box hammering
      179 SYNs in a pre-arena reconnect loop - real but distinct; its reaps never
      touched room 53). Starfighter = account Dutchwing, a clean session throughout.
      OPEN/NEXT: (a) confirm CREATE-ORDER shows create-first + no CTD on the retest;
      (b) the Shadow 179-SYN loop - _reap_stale_sessions reaps on EVERY re-SYN incl.
      a live session, worth a freshness guard; likely Shadow's own client/network.

