      ServerConfirm=257 -> client emits msg-59 (spawn ask) -> v480f5 logged
      'AIR-START arena - no spawn grant' and sent NO msg-60. Pilot then flew into
      the ground and the client CTD'd: messages33 shows 'Player crashed into
      ground', ExitEvent(257) Hits=-1, then 'Access violation ... 0x4050414D'
      (Main.cpp:2407). 0x4050414D is ASCII 'MAP@' - an uninitialised/garbage
      pointer; Hits=-1 is uninitialised damage tracking. i.e. the client STILL
      asks for supply at an air-start spawn and NEEDS the msg-60 reply to
      initialise plane loadout/damage state - it does NOT self-supply. Without it
      the death/exit path dereferences uninitialised memory -> CTD.
      * FIX: removed the air-start guard from _grant_spawn_supply; the spawn-59
        reply now fires for air-start rooms exactly as it did through v479f5
        (which never CTD'd here). The spawn reply is SOLICITED and safe; the
        Taurus cold-engine bug (v452f5, messages77) was the UNSOLICITED poll
        grant, which is still suppressed in air-start rooms via
        _grant_auto_resupply's explicit=False default.
      * KEPT from v480f5: 'part 1', the landing-repair fix - _grant_auto_resupply
        gains explicit=False and the msg-119 call site passes explicit=True, so a
        plane that LANDS in an air-start arena still repairs/rearms on request.
        Unaffected by this CTD (different path) and retained.
      NET after v481f5: air-start SPAWN -> normal spawn-59 grant (initialises the
      plane, no CTD); air-start LANDING + explicit 119 -> serviced; air-start POLL
      inference -> still suppressed. Ground-start rooms unchanged. FUTURE NOTE: if
      a TC air-start room ever shows cold-engine on the spawn grant specifically,
      the fix is to force the silent restore flags (0x06/0x07) for that grant, NOT
      to skip it - skipping is what caused this CTD.

v480f5 [RESUPPLY - AIR-START LANDING REPAIR + GUARD RELOCATION] Aircraft that
      landed at a field in an AIR-START arena (StartGround=no) could never repair
      or rearm on the ground. Local repro (messages32, StartGround=no StartAlt=
      1000m: client renders 'accepted to airfield' + emits out-119; run_213025
      21:35: msg-119 REFUSED airborne, then 'AIR-START arena - no spawn grant').
      Contrast run_205133 (ground-start TC): the identical ground-stop path
      granted 'TC FULL loadout-restore' every time. Root cause: the v452f5 air-
      start skip was placed in _grant_auto_resupply, which is NOT the spawn path -
      it is the LANDING path, reached ONLY from the explicit msg-119 request
      (_handle_repair_request_119) and the ground-stop poll. So the guard (a)
      never protected the spawn grant it was written for, and (b) blocked every
      legitimate landing repair for the whole life of the room.
      * _grant_auto_resupply(s, pos, explicit=False): the air-start skip is now
        gated on `not explicit`, so it is a POLL-ONLY guard against the just-
        spawned airborne false ground-stop (the Taurus cold-engine case). The
        msg-119 call site passes explicit=True - the client only emits 0x77 after
        it locally accepts an airfield, so it is the authority that it is parked;
        the path's own airborne guard (movement >= REPAIR_119_AIRBORNE_MIN=4000)
        still refuses a genuine mid-air 119. Poll site keeps the default -> still
        suppressed in air-start rooms (spawn-grace + ground_stop_eligible remain).
      * _grant_spawn_supply: the air-start skip now lives HERE too, at the top of
        the actual spawn (msg-59 reply) path - so a spawn-time msg-60 no longer
        runs 'Fueling and Arming' on the 1000m airborne spawn. This closes the
        latent case seen in run_213025 21:33:10 ('spawn-59 -> ARCADE full service'
        firing unguarded in an air-start FFA). Air-start planes spawn fuelled/
        armed, so no spawn service is wanted; a plane that later LANDS is serviced
        via the 119/poll path, which no longer carries the skip.
      Net: air-start spawn -> no grant; air-start landing + explicit 119 -> full
      service; air-start poll inference -> still suppressed. Ground-start rooms
      unchanged. NOT yet field-tested - verify next session: an air-start room
      should show 'msg-119 repair REQUEST -> granting' followed by a real SUPPLY60
      where it previously logged 'AIR-START arena ... no spawn grant'.

v479f5 [SPAWN-STATE - THE 97% LOADING FREEZE] Taurus froze at 97% entering
      Two Islands II (messages23, run_140046). NOT a render hang and NOT a
      slow load: FA.exe RE (FUN_0046ae70, Msn_Serv.cpp) shows the client gates
      its StartPlace ask on a one-bit state, p->WaitingForStartPlace
      (piVar5[0x6aa]) - set when it asks, cleared ONLY after it processes a
      usable grant. A SECOND grant arriving while the bit is still set makes
      the next ask assert '!p->WaitingForStartPlace' - FATAL in the Developer
      build = the freeze. Ask sender is RealSendAskStartPlace (FUN_004fcbd0);
      payload builder FUN_004fd5b0 emits [af][place][0xff] triplets - the
      protocol is strict request->response, one grant per ask. Log proof:
      Taurus's FAILED grant (14:09:18) came via the COMPOUND/scan path
      (cmd=0x1203) while mid-load and was followed by NO msg-59/SUPPLY60
      (spawn never completed, 140s dead air then relog); his SUCCESSFUL
      15:19 grant was a bare/clean ask followed by the normal SUPPLY60. Under
      latency+load the client compound-BATCHES its ask, so the same ask can
      reach us twice within ms and we answered both -> two grants, one flag.
      * Part 1 (solicited-only): confirmed all 6 handle_fly_start_place call
        sites are ask-driven; the ONLY eager path is the v462 death-re-grant,
        which is already heavily guarded (cancels on hangar/flying/respawn,
        6s delay, 2 field rescues) - left as-is, not ripped out.
      * Part 2 (de-dup): handle_fly_start_place drops an identical ask
        (af,mid,n,reply_sub) seen within SP_ASK_DEDUP_S=0.75s - catches the
        compound-batch duplicate, never a real re-ask seconds later (the
        client's own RealSendAskStartPlace retry is on a seconds cadence).
      * Part 3 (SPAWN-WATCH, observation only): the _stall_watch loop now
        logs a GRANT that never became a spawn (no flying/msg-59 within
        SP_CONFIRM_WATCH_S=12s) with the channel state + a flightrec dump, so
        the next occurrence is hard data. Deliberately does NOT re-grant - a
        blind re-grant is itself the unsolicited grant Parts 1+2 exist to
        stop. NOTE: this is a mitigation; the true cure (client not dropping
        a grant received mid-load) is in the exe. Watch for SPAWN-WATCH lines
        after deploy to confirm the de-dup caught the batch case.

v478f5 [SESSION - PRE-ARENA GHOST / DOUBLE-LOBBY] Taurus@HQ (acct Sinistarr,
      340ms link) stuck at pilot select, appeared TWICE in the lobby, then
      timed out (messages27/28, run_152706). Root cause is NOT server-side:
      his first reliable DATA arrived 15.47s after SYN (the server auth-ACKed
      it in 71ms) - i.e. client-side plane preload + init on a slow path,
      brushing the client's own ~14s connect timeout (the long-open v351
      note). Not fixable server-side (would need the exe). But two server
      behaviours made it WORSE, both fixed:
      * DOUBLE-LOBBY: a high-latency client whose advancing response was lost
        re-sends pilot-select every few seconds; the 0x62/0xe4 handler re-ran
        the FULL join each time, re-broadcasting '[x] has joined the lobby' +
        broadcast_player_join -> same pilot shown twice. Fix: re-selection of
        the SAME pilot on the SAME pre-arena session is now idempotent -
        re-sends the advancing responses (MyRights, UI lists, echo) so the
        stuck client can unstick itself, but skips the one-time join
        broadcasts. First selection unchanged.
      * PRE-ARENA GHOST not reaped: _reap_stale_sessions enforces one-
        connection-per-account, but only fires on a NEW SYN - Taurus's stuck
        client kept retrying on its OLD session (last_rx stayed fresh, so the
        idle reaper's silence test never caught it) and didn't re-SYN for 4
        min. Fix: the idle-reaper loop now ALSO reaps duplicate-account
        sessions continuously - when two live authed sessions share an
        account, the older t0 is the ghost and is torn down (DUP-REAP),
        keeping only the newest connection. Decision made under sl; lone
        sessions never touched. Enforces the one-per-account invariant
        between SYNs, not just at them.

v477f5 [ARENA-LIST + IMPERSONATION + GAMEDEF PACING TUNABLE]
