v476f5 [ARENA-LIST LATENCY - GAME_DEF STORM] The in-game arena tab took 3-4s
      and 'refreshed multiple times' (NOT the web page - that was WEBPERF/
      v475). The client POLLS 0xd2 ~1/s to keep the tab fresh; each poll
      re-ran send_arenalist_with_gamedefs, re-streaming all 9 rooms' 212
      GAME_DEF blobs at 120ms pacing = ~1.1s of GAME_DEF storm PER POLL,
      overlapping so the list never settled. (The first suspect, the 213
      counts-reply pacing, was a red herring - v476f5 made those concurrent,
      harmless but not the cause.) Fix chain:
      * f5b: GAME_DEFs primed ONCE per session - tracked in s._gamedef_sent
        keyed by a hash of the stored blob, re-sent only on first sight or
        when the blob changed (web edit). A refresh poll now costs just the
        0xd2 list + concurrent counts (~one RTT). v455 anti-CTD pacing kept,
        paid only on the first prime.
      * f5c: per-session lock around the prime - the client fires ~5 polls in
        the first ~350ms of opening the tab, which raced on _gamedef_sent and
        re-primed; the lock serializes so exactly one prime happens.
      Result (user): 'much faster for good connections, page more responsive.'
      Remaining first-open floor is the pacing itself -> v477 tunable.

v475f5 [WEB/ARENAS - PERF INSTRUMENTATION + PERSISTENT FLAG + CLEANUP]
