v469f5 [STATLOSS + TELEM8-TRANS - TWO INSTRUMENTS, ONE VERSION]
      * STATLOSS: parse the client's STATUS REPLY (subtype-4, previously
        ignored; non-returning insert in on_pkt so piggybacked ACK sections
        are untouched) against the deltas we packed into the matching STATUS
        -> per-client DIRECTIONAL loss (downlink = our sent vs their recvd;
        uplink = their sent vs our recvd) with EWMA(1/8) + running totals.
        The EWMA is the phantom-vs-real separator: in-flight skew alternates
        +/- and sums ~0 (run_195327: skew +1,-1,+5,-5,+2,-2, sum=2 = the only
        2 real losses in 155 intervals on Alon's 0.35s link - downlink 0.00%,
        uplink 0.14%); real loss is one-sided and settles the EWMA at its
        rate. Phantom amplitude ~ uplink_rate x RTT - THE explanation for
        'most players show D: even at 0.05' (physics, not the server; kernel
        confirms: netstat -su = 0 rcv/snd buffer errors at 13.1M/50.3M pkts).
      * TELEM8-TRANS: capture a 07->08->07 sequence per emitter (max 2/
        session) - consecutive frames share flight state, so the byte-diff
        localizes the 0x08 insert exactly (the v461 FIRST-frame dumps were
        minutes apart and would not align). Paid off next session.
      * (Initial reply-offset assumption wrong - see v470/v471.)

