v455f5 [GAMEDEF/REPAIR - CRITICAL OFFSET CORRECTION + 212 pacing] The user
      uploaded the ONLINE box's production fa_server.db (19 rooms); dry-
      running the v453f5 migration against it exposed that the v450f5
      repair-rate offset derivation was WRONG:
      * REALITY (19/19 blobs): bytes at aa-5..aa-1 = [0,100,100,100,100] =
        [BuildingDamage, BuildingsArmor, BuildingsScore, BuildingsLife,
        BuildingsRepairRate] - the ScoreAndDamage tail runs DIRECTLY into
        the 5 AA-quality bytes; the [AI] bools are NOT on the wire there
        (they sit earlier in the walk). So BuildingsRepairRate = aa-1, not
        aa-5. The old 4-bools guard saw [100,100,100,100] and REFUSED every
        real blob: the serve patch and migration were harmless no-ops that
        would never have fixed anything. (This also retroactively explains
        why nothing was ever corrupted despite the wrong offset.)
      * FIX: apply_buildings_repair_rate + migrate_stored_gamedefs_repair_
        rate both patch aa-1, guarded by the AA-quality shape (5 bytes all
        0..10 - the same trust apply_aa_quality uses on top of the full
        deserializer-replay locator).
      * PRODUCTION-PROVEN: dry-run on the uploaded DB: 19/19 rooms located
        rate=100 at aa-1 (several rooms show real AA qualities 6/1/3/1/1
        etc., EvP-silent rooms all-zero - guard shape holds either way);
        19/19 patched copies fa_compress round-trip byte-exact. The
        migration will bake 0 into every stored arena on first v455f5
        start.
      * messages04_1_ CTD FOLLOW-UP: all 19 stored blobs pass the FULL
        deserializer walk (aa located, startground located, identical 710B
        tail after AA) and client-exact camps validation - stored data is
