v448f5 [PVE/GROUND - THE MAPPING, SOLVED OFFLINE] Terrain tables decoded from
      the binary; live-memory extractor written; server consumes the dump as
      the authoritative obj->scene source.
      * TERRAIN LOADER FULLY DECOMPILED (FUN_0055f040, Trn.cpp): the client
        builds each world from five flat tables in its archives, all kept
        behind fixed globals (base 0x400000, no ASLR):
          gst SCENE_TYPE_DEF        0x30B  ptr@0xc85028 cnt@0xc84fec (names)
          gat AIRFIELD_TYPE_DEF     0x10B  ptr@0xc8502c cnt@0xc84ff0
          got GROUND_OBJECT_TYPE_DEF 0xc0B ptr@0xc85030 cnt@0xc84ff4
              (+0xa0 s32 Value >0=destructible <0=decoration-skip; +0xb0
               radius; +0xb4 category; +0xbc destroy-mode byte: 2=never,
               1=local-kill - FUN_00568eb0)
          gsi SCENE_INST_DEF        0x18B  ptr@0xc85034 cnt@0xc84ff8
              (+0 scene-type; +4 flags LOW NIBBLE = CAMP; +8/+0xc x/y)
          goi GROUND_OBJECT_INST_DEF 0x2cB ptr@0xc85038 cnt@0xc84ffc
              (+0 TypeIndex->got; +4 SceneInstIndex->gsi = THE OBJ->SCENE
               MAPPING; +8/+0xc x/y)
        PARR<TRN_SCENE*> (0xc87268/0xc8726c) is created size=nSceneInst and
        filled IN gsi ROW ORDER -> the msg-36 scene index IS the gsi row.
        PARR<TRN_OBJECT*> (0xc87270/0xc87274) filled IN goi ROW ORDER -> the
        msg-31 object index IS the goi row. The client's startup 'Info TRNnn
        - scenes with valuable objects' print IS the gsi enumeration
        (col0=gsi idx, col1=camp, col2=sum of got values, col3=gst name) -
        so TRN02 room 49: 46 0 2995 Front Airfield = the user's target;
        33 0 2835 Bomber Airfield.
      * FILE-OPEN CHAIN (FUN_0042e820 -> FUN_007db550 -> FUN_007dde70): the
        client tries the REAL filesystem FIRST ('Trn02\table.gsi' relative
        to the game dir - modding override possible!), then the packed VFS.
        No Trn02 dir exists on disk; the tables live in Data00..08.all
        (format still un-RE'd; q6 volumes proven NOT to contain them). The
        memdump route makes the container format unnecessary.
      * fa_dump_trn_tables.py (NEW, reuses fa_memdump.py plumbing): attaches
        read-only to the live FA.exe, reads the 5 ptr/count globals + terrain
