v443f5 [TC/SUPPLY] PER-RESOURCE SUPPLY GRANTS - 'check the scene supply status
      first, then resupply accordingly' (field spec 2026-08-15). The pool draw
      IS the check: _tc_pool_draw (shared by spawn-59 / msg-119 / ground-stop
      poll) draws the ask atomically and every grant is composed from what each
      resource ACTUALLY yielded - closing the old peek->take race and making
      destroyed storage bite per-resource (a killed fuel depot zeroes its
      stores v291 + produces nothing at efficiency 0.0, so the fuel side of
      the next draw comes up short -> 'Fuel limited to' - and same for ammo
      dumps -> 'Ammunition limited to').
      * SPAWN (_grant_spawn_supply): ammo keeps the field-proven v438f5 bit0
        budget-reload (+1.5s rack delay), but the ask now SCALES WITH THE
        AIRFRAME: is_bomber_plane(s.plane_type) -> 1500kg budget vs 500kg
        fighter - THE 'no bombs/rockets even though the base can supply them'
        FIX (a rich base answering a B-17 with a 500kg cap under-armed the
        heavy racks; the budget is a cap the client loads up to, debit = what
        the pool yielded). Fuel goes per-resource: bit1 loadout-fill only when
        the pool covered SUPPLY_TC_FUEL_ADD_KG; short -> bit1 clear, bit0
        routes 'Fuel limited to <yield>'. bit3 narration only when MEANING-
        FULLY short (below the classic 500 rearm cost, not below the generous
        bomber budget - no false shortage on fighter spawns).
      * MID-LIFE (_grant_auto_resupply, feeding both the poll and msg-119):
        per-resource matrix, bit0 NEVER (the v427f5 ordnance-stripper hazard
        on loaded planes): both covered -> 0x06 silent total restore (out-73);
        fuel-only -> 0x0a (bit1 loadout fuel + incremental ammo add + bit3);
        ammo-only -> 0x0c (bit2 full guns/ordnance + incremental fuel + bit3);
        both short -> 0x08 incremental yields. The LEAN 150kg ammo cap is gone
        - 'arm according to what CAN be allocated at the time'.
      * SUPPLY_TC_SPAWN_AMMO_FIGHTER_KG=500 / _BOMBER_KG=1500 added;
        SPAWN59_FLAGS + SUPPLY_TC_AMMO_ADD_KG retired to reference.
      NOTE plane_type: out-4 byte[8]; v201's comment says nation-ordinal but
      months of cross-nation peer rendering (creates carry it) + the v242
      Fighter/Bomber scoring treat it as the global roster id - is_bomber_plane
      uses it exactly as the scoring path does.

v442f5 [WIRE/CRITICAL] RELIABLE TX OUTSTANDING CAP (the seq-runaway downlink
      wedge = flak's HQ blankout mechanism) + THIRD EXIT-SITE KEPT + msg-7
      NEVER ECHOED (the solo in 7'84) + TX/TELEM7 instrument.
      * (A) REL_MAX_OUTSTANDING=160: the client's reliable QRcv is mod-512 with
        a fatal window - offset 0x100 from a stuck nExpected is 'Sequence Error
        -> queue out of range' and the downlink is POISONED (v371f5 RE). The
        client ACKs in order, so ONE lost send freezes nExpected and every new
        send widens the gap. GCP field case (run_20260814_214810, flakmagic
        00:47:53-00:48:26): leave -> one lost reply -> 1Hz 0x43 re-polls each
        answered with ~10 reliable sends (0xd2 + 6x213 + counts) -> gap crossed
        the window exactly as his TX seq crossed 511 (00:48:06.677, the second
        his client went silent; 77 healthy crossings that night harmless).
        FIX: send_rel refuses NEW sends (no seq allocated, TX/RELCAP log, 5s
        rate-limited) while len(_evts) >= 160 un-ACKed. Lossy only for an
        already-deaf client, and every reliable payload is a re-requested
        answer, re-stated idempotent state, or keeper-backed handshake - the
        cap is what makes RECOVERY possible (keeper lands the head, client
        drains, ACKs flow, _evts empties, sends resume). Bonus: the keeper's
        'KNOWN LIMIT' (seq reuse re-keying a held event after 512 sends) is now
        unreachable.
      * (B) THIRD exit-appspace site (scan-inner type=0x40 cmd=5) no longer
        does a bare closing+sids.pop on an ACK timeout - session KEPT, same as
        the two v441f5 sites. That bare pop was the harshest of the three (no
        teardown broadcast at all -> instant ghost + peers never told).
      * (C) 0x07 (msg-7 TELEMETRY) added to NO_ECHO_SUBS + the compound tuple:
        telemetry arriving on the RELIABLE channel (wrapped internet forms /
        occasional reliable-channel frames) fell through to the generic echo -
        the sender received its OWN telemetry back (the solo 'in 7'84' stream,
        messages62; relay_telemetry only ever ran on the unreliable path, so
        peers never depended on the echo - swallow is a pure fix). The v440f5
        cmd=546 guard already carried 0x07.
      * (D) TX/TELEM7 instrument in send_unrel: one log per (session,label)
        when an outbound unreliable payload parses as an opcode-7 frame - if
        any 'in 7' reflection survives (C), the label names the sender.

