v440f5 [CTD/CRITICAL] EXIT-TO-HQ CTD: THE cmd=546 BLIND ECHO (+ TX poison filter
      + death-form msg-59 ignore).
      Field (messages62 / run_20260815_003043, 00:33:08, solo 'Nations at war'
      dogfight room): player parked -> exit to HQ -> instant CTD, engine dump
      'bounds error ARR<NET::OBJECT*,2048>[65535] 0..2047' (ring.hpp:27), last
      inbound 'in 33'8' 30-60ms after its own 'out 33'8'.
      CHAIN: v438f5b stamps Dogfighting rooms Type=1 'Mission' -> exit-to-HQ now
      runs Msn_Exit and emits ExitEvent(-1) - msg-33, Number=0xFFFF - during the
      HQ transition on the 546 channel: [ctr][ctr][02][22][21][b1][ff][ff][ty].
      THE POISON BYTES DEFEAT THE PREFIX DETECTOR: _pfx requires pl[6:8]==0000,
      but Number=0xFFFF sits exactly at pl[6:8], so the frame skipped every
      REFRAME/NO_ECHO guard, fell into the cmd==0x0222 branch (len 12 < 15) and
      hit its UNCONDITIONAL echo - which had NO log() call (send_rel label only),
      i.e. invisible at every loglevel. The client indexed ring[65535] and died.
      This was the LAST unguarded echo (v222 sub-byte, v222 type-byte, v360f5
      compound tuple, v411f5 prefixed-reframe all guarded their own paths).
      FIXES:
      * (A) cmd=546 NO-ECHO GUARD: before the echo, detect the carried message id
        (pl[6:8]==0000 -> well-formed inner, id at pl[8]; else raw/poison shape,
        id at pl[4]) and SWALLOW ids in NO_ECHO_SUBS + 0x07, log tag ECHO546.
        pl[4] is only tested in the malformed shape, so pilot-management echoes
        (whose inner bc can legitimately be 0x03+) are untouched.
      * (B) _tx_poison_33() TX CHOKE-POINT FILTER in send_rel + send_unrel: an
        outbound frame parseable as msg-33 with Number=0xFFFF is BLOCKED and
        logged (tag TX-POISON33) with the send label - covers every known and
        UNKNOWN path at the last exit before the socket; the server's own 14B
        credit (small PlayerIndex, no ff ff) passes. Relay sendto (peers) keeps
        its own v360f5 window guard.
      * (C) DEATH/EXIT-form msg-59 IGNORED: the client also emits msg-59 at
        life-teardown with plane fields 0xFF (...3e04 ffffffffffffffff vs the
        spawn form's live data). v438f5 treated it as a spawn ask and fired a
        msg-60 grant 1.5s later into a client sitting on the HQ page
        (entered_game/my_obj_number do NOT flip on a plain exit, so the delayed-
        grant guards passed) - the ACE88/v416f5 hazard class. Now detected
        (trailing 8 bytes all 0xFF) -> no grant, no debounce; delayed grant also
        aborts on s.closing.
