v435f5 [RESUPPLY] MSG-119 REPAIR REQUEST IS NOW THE PRIMARY SUPPLY TRIGGER - the client asks,
      the server grants, instead of the server inferring 'parked' from telemetry.
      DECODE (run_20260813_203929 SUPPLY-CAP, type=0x52 sub=0x77): msg 119 = 0x77, the client's
      repair/resupply request. Wire form (sub already unwrapped by v327/v364f5):
        direct   len 9:  00 52 00 00 77 [ctr] 00 [fl] 00
        prefixed len 13: [ctr u16][0542] + the same 9 bytes
      byte5 = per-pilot request counter (a nonce); byte7 = 00 normally, 04 on the client's own
      unanswered-retry. No parameters we need - it means 'service me now'. Proof it is the
      request: every 0x77 that preceded a grant had flying=True; the only unanswered ones were
      Taurus's first-landing failures (flying=False, byte7=04 retries) - i.e. the client WAS
      asking on that first landing and the server ignored it (no 119 handler existed, and the
      v434f5 poll gate had skipped him).
      WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT MODEL: the client renders 'accepted to airfield' locally and only
      then sends 0x77, so it is the authority on whether it is serviceable. Granting on request
      retires the entire ground-stop-INFERENCE class of bugs that produced v277 (stale-view mid-
      air rearm), v346 (tick-freeze false-static), v422f5 (bail/respawn airborne grants), and
      v434f5 (flying-gate first-landing miss) - all of them were the server trying to guess a
      fact the client already knew.
      HANDLER (_handle_repair_request_119): grants via the existing _grant_auto_resupply (arcade
      0x07 / TC tiers unchanged), guarded by entered_game + obj_confirmed + spawn-grace + a light
      AIRBORNE guard (refuse only if plane_movement != 0, so a malformed/hostile request cannot
      trigger a mid-air rearm) + the shared one-shot/debounce so it cannot double-grant with the
      poll. plane_movement==0 (parked OR no-evidence) with the client asserting a field = grant.
      The v422f5 ground-stop background poll is RETAINED as a fallback for any client that does
      not ask; shared resupplied_this_stop/_grant_pos/last_resupply_at keep the two paths from
      double-granting.
      FALSIFY: land (or Ctrl+Tab to a field) and stop -> the client's out-119 draws an immediate
      grant; server logs 'msg-119 repair REQUEST -> granting'. First landing after launch now
      works with no tab. Airborne/taxiing 0x77 (if any) logs 'REFUSED - plane moving'. Retry
      spam while parked is absorbed by debounce (one grant per stop). REVERT: remove the
      _handle_repair_request_119 dispatch line; the poll alone resumes (v434f5 behaviour).

==============================================================================

v434f5 [RESUPPLY] GROUND-STOP POLL GATED ON obj_confirmed, NOT flying - fixes "repair does
      not work on the first landing; had to Ctrl+Tab to get repaired".
      DIAGNOSED FROM THE SERVER LOG (run_20260813_203929.log, account Sinistarr / pilot
      Taurus@HQ, FFA):
        21:02:26  Taurus obj 0x0104 DAMAGED by 0x0105
        21:03:38  FLY23 StartPlace tab to AF4 -> GRANT N=0; from here flying=False (parked,
                  never took off from this field), client sends its repair-poll heartbeat
                  type=0x52 sub=0x77 with flying=False
        21:03:38-21:05:40  parked & damaged ~2 min, ZERO RESUPPLY grants
        21:05:40  HD75@FA destroyed Taurus (killed while parked) - lost plane + life
        21:12:44  next life: took off first (flying=True), landed, sat -> RESUPPLY fired
                  normally, and did so on every subsequent life (all flying=True).
      ROOT CAUSE: _resupply_poll_loop skipped any session with flying=False
      (`not getattr(s,'flying',False) -> continue`). flying is True ONLY after a
      ServerConfirm-with-takeoff (L10350) and is cleared on every StartPlace/tab and on death
      (L8813/L10692). So a plane that Ctrl+Tabs to a field - or spawns at one - and PARKS
      without first taking off has flying=False and was excluded from the very poll meant to
      service grounded planes. The client's repair-poll heartbeat (type=0x52 sub=0x77, the
      out-119 in the client log) fires in BOTH states; only the server's flying gate differed,
      which is why a Ctrl+Tab that ended in a normal takeoff+land 'fixed' it.
      FIX: gate the poll on obj_confirmed instead of flying. A spawn-confirmed plane is
      serviceable whether or not it ever took off; ground_stop_eligible() still requires fresh
      onum-matched telemetry with an advancing conductor tick, and the spawn-grace window still
      guards the mid-build case, so nothing airborne/half-built slips through. entered_game +
      obj_confirmed + my_obj_number remain required.
      FALSIFY: spawn OR Ctrl+Tab onto an airfield, take damage, land WITHOUT a prior takeoff,
      sit with brakes on -> RESUPPLY grant within ~SETTLE+poll, no tab needed. Regression:
      normal takeoff->land->park still grants exactly once per stop; airborne planes still
      never grant (movement!=0). REVERT: restore the `or not getattr(s,'flying',False)` disjunct.
      NOTE: pairs with v433f5 (repair clears the damage latch) - together, land-repair-exit is
      now clean whether the pilot took off first or tabbed straight to a field.

