v433f5 [KILL/SCORE] REPAIR CLEARS THE DAMAGE LATCH - fixes "land, repair, exit -> lose a
      plane and a life; last shooter gets a phantom kill + cyan banner".
      FIELD BUG (Taurus, messages57_1_.log, FFA Two Islands, 2026-08-13):
        18:46:38  HitFrom(518) hits Taurus mid-sortie          -> took_damage=True, PENDING_KILL set
        18:47:05  ServerConfirm obj 521 (Taurus, Yak-3)
        ...dogfights, more HitFrom...
        18:55:37  "You are accepted to this airfield" (serviced)
        18:56:18  HitFrom(524) + ExitEvent(521) IsDelete=1 MEC=21 ScoreEvent=3  -> booked a DEATH,
                  attacker 524 (Camp=4, enemy) credited the kill with the cyan PLAYER_KILLED banner.
      ROOT CAUSE: took_damage (set on every msg-28, ~L12660) and PENDING_KILL (the no-clock kill
      latch, ~L12666) were cleared ONLY on a fresh spawn (spawn path L10422/L10430). REPAIR never
      cleared them, so damage taken earlier in a life stayed latched through a full field repair;
      the exit classifier's `_damaged` branch (~L10604) then counted the normal exit as a damaged
      death and score_on_death handed the last shooter the kill. The exit-tail was synthesised
      (short form) so v372f5's ANNOUNCE_SYNTH_KILL printed the cyan banner too - the "other player
      got the kill with a cyan message" symptom.
      FIX: send_supply_grant_60() now clears took_damage + pops PENDING_KILL for the serviced
      plane, and drops _pos_hist (a repaired plane is parked/fresh, so the movement crash-test
      must not read the pre-repair flight). A msg-60 grant is the server's own statement that the
      plane is airworthy again, which is exactly when the latch should retire. This is the single
      choke point for every auto-resupply repair (arcade 0x07 and TC tiers all route through it).
      A plane hit AGAIN after repair re-latches via the normal msg-28 path, so a genuine post-
      repair kill still counts. Guarded by REPAIR_CLEARS_DAMAGE_LATCH (True); False = old behaviour.
      FALSIFY: take damage, land, get the auto-repair grant (RESUPPLY log line), then exit to HQ:
        server logs 'obj 0xNNNN REPAIRED -> damage latch + PENDING_KILL cleared', DEATH log says
        'exited UNDAMAGED ... clean exit, NOT a death', no score change, no cyan banner on the
        shooter. Regression check: get hit, repair, then get SHOT DOWN again -> still a death,
        killer still credited (the re-latch from the new msg-28 works).
      OPEN/RELATED (not changed here, watch for it): if a pilot lands and exits in a mode/arena
      where the auto-repair grant does NOT fire (no msg-60 sent), took_damage is still live and the
      same phantom-death occurs. If that shows up, mirror this clear on the airfield-accept (msg-23
      "accepted to this airfield") path as well. Current fix covers every case where a repair grant
      is actually issued, which is the reported scenario.

