v431f5: [TC] FIX v430f5 PANEL FLOOD - msg-69 is a POLL, not an open-event; debounce the push.
      v430f5 field test (run_20260812_170450.log) exposed the flaw: the client sends the msg-69
      SCENE_SUPPLY query ~25-30x PER SECOND the whole time the panel is open (always the same
      scene-set, e.g. 5/30/55). v430f5 fired a full 42->40->71 sequence on EVERY poll ->
        * FLOOD: ~900 SUPPLY69/PANELSEQ lines in a few seconds; wire saturated.
        * PANEL FLICKER: the client alternated 'unknown damage' <-> '0%' because the arena-wide
          msg-42 SCENE SNAPSHOT was being re-ingested 30x/sec, so the panel was perpetually
          mid-rebuild and never settled to show data.
      ROOT CAUSE: treated a continuous poll as a one-shot event, and put an ARENA-WIDE message
      (42) on the per-scene hover path. Both wrong.
      FIX:
        * _maybe_push_panel(): DEBOUNCE. Push 40+71 to the querying session at most once per
          PANEL_DEBOUNCE (3s) per (session, scene-set); a genuine change of hovered scene re-
          pushes immediately, holding still does not. Unit-tested: 30 polls/s -> 1 push; scene
          change -> re-push; per-session isolated.
        * DROPPED msg-42 from the hover path entirely - it is arena-wide and belongs to
          join/ownership-change, not a scene hover. Panel push is now 40 (complex) + 71 (scene)
          only.
        * SUPPLY69 log line rate-limited to once / 5s per (session, scene-set) (SUPPLY69_LOG_GAP)
          so the run log stays readable; the 3-byte 69 REPLY is still sent on every poll (the
          client needs it).
      Gates: PANEL_OPEN_SEQUENCE (False = reply-only, pre-v430), PANEL_DEBOUNCE=3.0,
      SUPPLY69_LOG_GAP=5.0.
      STILL UNKNOWN (the original question): whether 40+71 actually FILL the panel. v430f5's
      flood prevented a clean read - the panel never settled long enough to tell. v431f5 makes
      the push stable and rare; if the panel is STILL blank with a clean single push, then the
      msg-71 array->column mapping is the culprit (still an unproven 'best guess') and the next
      step is the wire capture, not more blind pushing. If it now shows data, we're done.
      FALSIFY: open panel on a TC map -> log shows ONE 'PANELSEQ .. 40 xN -> 71 xM' per few
         seconds (not a flood), damage% is STABLE (no unknown<->0% flicker), and the Production
         Complex + Single Scene sections either populate (win) or stay blank (-> probe next).
      FIELD RESULT (run_20260812_171314.log): flood GONE, damage% STABLE, clean single pushes
         ('40 x1 -> 71 x3'). BUT panel still shows NO supply data. So the flood was masking the
         real blocker, now cleanly isolated: the client accepts 40+71 and renders nothing.
         RULED OUT this pass: msg-73 (0x49) is NOT the panel request - it's SendRepairInfo
         (msg73_decode_notes.md), a plane fuel/ammo report after a msg-60 grant; the 0x49 in the
         log is just the auto-resupply report, unrelated to the panel.
         CONCLUSION: the msg-71 array->column mapping (scene_prodinfo_arrays, still a documented
         'best guess') is the prime suspect. Added PANEL_PROBE + `panelprobe` console toggle:
         flips the panel push to send PRODINFO_PROBE marker families (A=0xA1BE.. .. I=0x99BE..)
         so we can READ which array feeds which on-screen column. Works now because the push is
         clean (v430's probe 'never reached the client' - likely the same flood this fix removes).
         NEXT RUN: console `panelprobe on`, open the panel in-game, note which column shows which
         marker family, report back -> pin the real mapping -> panel fills. `panelprobe off`
         restores real values.

