v430f5: [TC] SUPPLY LINKS (live-learned) + TICK HEARTBEAT + PANEL-OPEN SEQUENCE (blank-panel attempt).
      Three things, following the 2026-07-19 Production Complex screenshot as ground truth
      ('Link range: 21'; complex Metal 39,690 = 6 x single-scene 6,615; Single Scene Stored
      3,308 / Cap 6,615 = 50%).
      1) SUPPLY LINKS, learned LIVE from the client (no coordinates needed). Scene positions are
         not in any data we have (data00_scenes.json has a per-scene link RADIUS of 10000 but no
         x/y). We don't need them: the msg-69 panel query LISTS every scene the client considers
         linked into that complex. _handle_scene_supply_query_69 now records that id-set via
         record_link_group() (union-find fuse on overlap); complex_totals() aggregates stored +
         capacity over the linked scenes and units over their camps. linked_scenes_for() returns
         a scene's complex, falling back to itself until a group is observed. Unit-tested: groups
         fuse across anchors, totals sum correctly (matches the screenshot's 6x aggregate).
      2) TICK HEARTBEAT. The production tick ran silently (only PROD40, which is gated off for
         ambient) so 'no production ticks' in the log was a VISIBILITY gap, not a dead loop.
         Added a SUPPLYTICK line each step: '#N rooms=.. scenes=.. units[rID:a/t/s ..]'. Gated by
         SUPPLY_TICK_LOG; counter _SUPPLY_TICK_N.
      3) PANEL-OPEN SEQUENCE - the working hypothesis for the LONG-STANDING panel-blank blocker
         (documented open since ~v300: client accepts 42/40/71 but renders nothing when they
         arrive standalone). The msg-69 query IS the panel-open event, so on it we now push, to
         the querying session only, spaced by PANEL_SEQ_GAP: 42 SCENE SNAPSHOT (bind ownership)
         -> 40 PRODUCTION COMPLEX per camp in the queried complex (bind aggregate) -> 71 per-
         scene INFO for the queried scenes (bind detail). Best-effort in a daemon thread so it
         can never break the 69 reply the client is waiting on. Gates: PANEL_OPEN_SEQUENCE (set
         False to revert to reply-only), PANEL_SEQ_GAP=0.15. Builders validated to correct sizes
         against the screenshot's values (42=8B, 40=38B, 71=7+N*83).
      HONEST STATUS: (1) and (2) are done + tested. (3) is an ATTEMPT at a blocker that predates
         all this work - if the panel is still blank after it, the next lever is a wire capture
         of our 42/40/71 vs the client's post-query expectation (the PANELSEQ + PROD71 log lines
         are there to diagnose), NOT more guessing at the msg-71 array->column mapping (still a
         'best guess'; the last probe never reached the client). msg-71 arrays remain unproven.
      FALSIFY (3): open the Production Complex panel in-game on a TC map -> log shows PANELSEQ
         '42 -> 40 xN -> 71 xM'; if the panel now shows Complex + Single Scene data, the ordering
         was the missing precondition. If still blank, capture the wire and compare.

v429f5: [PRODUCTION] THE UNITS LAYER - Metal -> aircraft/tank/ship units (wiki step 3-5).
      FIELD-CONFIRMED 2026-08-12 (run_20260812_103722.log): `production` console command on
      room 49 -> 'economy seeded (60 scenes)', msg 40 x5 camps to the in-game session, each
      carrying u=4/4/4 with real stored/capacity totals. Live on the deployed build.
      TWO BLOCKERS FOUND+FIXED when the first live test showed nothing:
        (1) broadcast_production_40 was hard-gated by SEND_PRODUCTION_40=False, so the console
            command (and any diagnostic) returned 0 instantly. Added force=True param; the
            console path forces past the ambient-broadcast gate, per-tick caller stays gated.
        (2) the economy was SPAWN-GATED: _SUPPLY only populated when a pilot parked at a field,
            so a fresh arena had an empty tick loop and nothing to broadcast. Added
            seed_room_economy() (idempotent - supply_state seeds on first touch, returns
            existing after) called by BOTH the tick loop (every active in-game room, before
            iterating) and the console command (seed + one on-demand units build so the panel
            shows live counts immediately, not 0/0/0 until the next 60s tick).
      Context first: the q6 client-data hunt for per-scene production numbers concluded this
      session (q6_reader_status.md, exhaustive) - the economy is NOT in the client. The VFS6B
      reader was fully cracked (180k names, all members, calibrate() retired) but the .prs/.prp/
      .pup tables do not exist in any volume; production was always server-side. So v429f5 is
      built on the MEMDUMP/RE model (FA_TC_economy.md), NOT on any extracted client file.
      WHAT CHANGED: the minute tick (_supply_tick_loop) ran only wiki stages 1-2 (resources
      produced + stored), which is why build_production_40 had always sent units=(0,0,0). Now
      after resources are stored, each camp runs stages 3-5: convert stored METAL into built-
      not-deployed UNITS (PMT_UNIT_PRODUCER consumes Metal, confirmed in FA.exe). Because the
      per-scene UNIT_PRODUCER_DEF (.pup, 24B, layout never pinned) is unavailable, the layer is
      a CAMP-LEVEL METAL-DERIVED AGGREGATE - faithful to the mechanic, honest about the one
      unknown (the conversion ratio is a TUNABLE ASSUMPTION, not an extracted constant).
        * Unit TYPE per camp derived from REAL scene type names we already have: Tank/Metal
          Factory -> tank, any Airfield -> aircraft, Port -> ship (a camp may build several).
        * Per tick per type: convert up to UNITS_PER_TICK_MAX units' worth of the camp's stored
          metal (UNIT_METAL_COST each) into units, capped at UNIT_CAP_PER_CAMP. Metal spent is
          DEBITED from the camp's scenes (producers first) so the metal economy stays conserved;
          any partial-unit remainder is refunded cap-respecting. Unit-tested: metal in ==
          units*cost out exactly (98000 -> 49 units, 0 leaked), caps honoured, kinds correct.
        * msg-40 PRODUCTION COMPLEX now carries the real (aircraft,tank,ship) counts instead of
          (0,0,0); PROD40 log line shows u=a/t/s. SEND_PRODUCTION_40 gating unchanged (still off
          for ambient broadcast; the `production` console command exercises it on demand).
      Knobs (all TUNABLE, centralised by _SUPPLY_UNITS): UNIT_METAL_COST=2000,
      UNIT_CAP_PER_CAMP=99, UNITS_PER_TICK_MAX=4. Calibrate against a live TC arena's Production
      Complex panel (the authoritative source now).
      FALSIFY: on a TC map, `production` console command after a few minute-ticks -> each camp
      that owns a factory/airfield/port shows nonzero units matching its metal spend, camp metal
      totals drop by exactly units_built*2000, units never exceed 99, and a camp with no live
      metal producer stops building once drained.
      NOT YET (deferred, non-blocking): stage 6 (deploying a unit draws fuel+ammo) is still the
      per-spawn msg-60 grant, not tied to the unit pool; supply-radius LINK pooling across
      connected scenes (topology) remains the next production sub-project.

