v427f5: [SUPPLY] TC GRANTS GO INCREMENTAL - debit == fill BY CONSTRUCTION - built on the
      msg-60 handler DECOMPILE (FA.exe 0x005581c0, function defined by Alon and read this
      session), which finally reconciles every probe and settles the semantics for good:
        * EVERY grant repairs: the handler's first act in all paths is subobj(plane+0x1F4)
          ->vfunc+0x20(full) - airframe restore. Repair was never bit0's.
        * bit1&bit2 together -> vfunc20(1) = TOTAL restore (loadout fuel + guns + ordnance),
          silent - what arcade's 0x07 executes, one call.
        * NO fill bits -> INCREMENTAL adds: FUN_004ebf50(amount) fuel, FUN_004ecad0(amount2)
          ammo - silent, no unload, no strip, amount 0 SAFE (shows 'no fuel/ammo
          available'). The mode v285 believed 0x08 was. It is flags 0x00.
        * bit3 -> two canned strings 0xe5/0xe6 ('insufficient aircraft units' / 'taking from
          tank production') - DISPLAY ONLY. v347 was right, v426f5's relabel wrong: there is
          NO client-side units stock. THE UNITS ECONOMY WAS ALWAYS SERVER-SIDE - the 2009
          server did the accounting and used bit3 to narrate its shortages. Full control.
        * bit0&!bit2's reload-to-budget is the ordnance STRIPPER - which is what 'denied the
          bombs on spawn' was: our v426f5 TC 0x03 grant fired on the freshly spawned parked
          bomber, unloaded every station and reloaded guns only. TC no longer sends bit0.

      TC POLICY NOW (arcade 0x07 unchanged):
        * RICH pool (ammo >= SUPPLY_TC_REARM_AMMO_KG=500): flags 0x04 - full guns AND
          ordnance + incremental fuel add; flat 500 kg ammo cost debited, fuel debit = add.
        * LEAN pool: flags 0x08 - incremental adds of exactly what the pool holds (capped at
          300 fuel / 150 ammo per stop), pool debited exactly that, plus bit3's authentic
          shortage narration for the ordnance not restored. Dry resource -> add 0, safe,
          client's own 'no fuel/ammo available' shows. The v425f5 [DRY] no-grant branch and
          its bookkeeping are gone.
        * Free airframe repair rides along on any grant (client behaviour, unavoidable);
          costing repairs in metal/aircraft-units is the next economy stage, now known to be
          purely server-side arithmetic + bit3 narration.

      FALSIFY: TC - spawn a bomber, park through the grace: bombs SURVIVE the grant. Rich
      pool: full rearm incl. racks, pool drops by 500+fuel. Drain the pool below 500: LEAN
