      FUN_004ec5c0 Plnprod.cpp rearm):
        * bit0 0x01 = repair + ABSOLUTE set: fuel := amount kg (clamped to tank capacity),
          guns unloaded then reloaded up to amount2 kg (clamped to plane ammo capacity).
          `resupply 0x01 0 0` = FULL DRAIN - a 0 amount under bit0 empties the plane. The
          v42xf5 'offer 0 when dry' design was therefore a plane-drainer; NEVER send 0.
        * bit1 0x02 = RESTORE-TO-LOADOUT: fuel to the pilot's HQ-selected loadout AND full
          ammo, silently, amounts ignored. v347 labelled this 'fuel to max' from the static
          read; the probe shows it restores the whole loadout (v283's matrix had seen the
          ammo effect and was dismissed). Combined with bit0 (0x03), bit1's fuel outcome
          WINS over bit0's amount (`resupply 0x03 50 1000` ends at loadout fuel, full ammo,
          only the ammo 'limited to 2205lb' message shown).
        * the 'supplied beyond the limits' report decoded: under 0x01 the DISPLAY prints the
          offer, the FILL is min(offer, capacity), and the DEBIT was the nominal 300/150 kg
          v285 leftover - three unrelated numbers. The fix is alignment, not clamping.

      POLICY (mode = scoring_mode_for_room(), web override wins as elsewhere):
        * ARCADE (ffa/events/none/custom): flags 0x23 (repair + loadout restore + ammo
          message suppressed), amount=100 (drain guard; bit1 overrides), amount2=0xffff
          (bomber ordnance fills too). Silent full service, no economy touched. Level 1.
        * TC: flags 0x03 - repair + fuel to LOADOUT (bit1; the loadout report fixed) + ammo
