      table for (RE task, filed). Every per-scene debit made through it - spawn OR landing -
      was against the wrong scene.

      FIX: camp_supply_take() drains the camp's profiled scenes, AIRFIELD-TYPED SCENES FIRST,
      production scenes after - which is the authentic mechanic in the client's own words:
      'insufficient aircraft units at the airfield, taking from tank production to supply'.
      Pilot's camp = s.nation; offers capped by the camp's remaining pool. On terrain 2 every
      camp owns Villages / Tank Factories holding 45-55k ammo, so the 'ammo 0 at spawn'
      symptom is gone by construction. Grant log carries [campN pool (M scenes)] + AFRAW=<id>
      (kept for the eventual start-place mapping).
      SUPPLY_CAMP_POOL=False reverts to the per-scene path, which also remains the automatic
      fallback for terrains without a SCENE_CAMP_BY_TERRAIN table and for camp-less sessions.

      NOTE ON SCOPE: scene DESTRUCTION effects are unchanged - v291's destroyed-scene store
      loss and per-scene HP/efficiency still act on the individual scene, and the camp pool
