v422f5: [RESUPPLY] AUTO-RESUPPLY RE-ENABLED behind a rewritten, FAIL-CLOSED ground-stop
      detector. It had been disabled on the live server because msg-60 grants kept firing at
      AIRBORNE aircraft.

      ROOT CAUSE (the compound v346 could not close): the gate stack judged freshness and
      "new packet" from last_telem_time - which is stamped for EVERY telemetry packet the
      session sends, ANY object - but took the position it judged from last_plane_telem,
      which updates ONLY when the packet's ONumber == my_obj_number. A bail (the parachuter
      transmits under its own number), a respawn's ONumber change, or the plane's own stream
      pausing while anything else keeps flowing => "fresh new packets" over a frozen cached
      position = reads as parked. Gate 4b then failed OPEN: plane_movement() returns 0 on NO
      EVIDENCE (correct for the crash classifier) and _pos_hist is cleared on every spawn, so
      the one predicate meant to catch the airborne case answered "parked" in precisely the
      divergence scenarios. Only the 10s spawn grace stood in the way.

      FIX - ground_stop_eligible(), ONE data path, no-evidence = NOT eligible:
        * judged solely from _pos_hist (samples appended only for ONumber==my_obj_number,
          each with its own arrival time; v422f5 adds the sender's conductor tick per sample
          - tuples grew to (t, pos, tick); plane_movement indexes [0]/[1], unaffected)
        * newest sample must be fresh BY ITS OWN TIMESTAMP (never the any-object clock)
        * plane_movement() over the retained window EXACTLY 0 (v346 calibration: parked=0
          sample after sample, airborne ~250k) - tested FIRST so a moving plane answers
          'movement=N', which is the ONLY answer that re-arms the one-shot (staleness or
          thin evidence must not, or a lossy link re-grants a plane that never moved =
          the v276 168-grants failure resurrected via packet loss)
        * >= AUTO_RESUPPLY_MIN_SAMPLES newest samples IDENTICAL in position, spanning
          >= AUTO_RESUPPLY_SETTLE seconds
        * the conductor tick must ADVANCE across the static run - a frozen conductor
          re-sending one stale state is indistinguishable from a parked plane by position
          alone; a genuinely parked client keeps ticking (type-7 flows when parked, v273).
          Closes v346's endemic tick-freeze false-static for good.

      ALSO CHANGED:
        * at_airfield NO LONGER GATES eligibility - it is ATTRIBUTION only (which field's
          stock a TC grant debits). A pilot whose StartPlace framing we fail to parse (the
          framing set has grown since v275: v340 re-frame, v364f5 universal unwrap)
          previously skipped at the poll's FIRST gate and could never resupply; now they get
          a blind [NO-AF] grant that debits nothing. This was also a latent None-crash:
          supply_take -> supply_state -> int(None) raised, and the poll's single try aborted
          the whole per-session scan for that tick.
        * the '0x53 engine-ON clears at_airfield' branch is GONE - v347 proved 0x53 is not
          engine state (...5300 precedes SPAWN, ...5301 precedes EXIT), so it fired at
          climb-OUT and never during a sortie. at_airfield := last spawn field, cleared on
          despawn (sub 0x03) only; _auto_resupply_check is slimmed to that maintenance and
          now runs regardless of AUTO_RESUPPLY.
        * one-shot re-arms on OBSERVED MOVEMENT or on parking at a DIFFERENT position
          (_grant_pos), instead of on any single changed poll sample.
        * per-SESSION try in the poll: one bad session no longer aborts the scan for the
          rest of that tick.
        * dead state removed: engine_on, parked_since, stationary_since, has_flown,
          last_pos, pos_static_since, pos_static_samples, last_pos_telem_t.
        * stale '(incremental)' tag dropped from the grant log line (flags are 0x01
          absolute-set since v347).

      KNOWN LIMIT (unchanged since v347, now the top of the resupply queue): at_airfield is
      the field you SPAWNED at. Land elsewhere and the wrong stock is debited (TC only).
      Position-based field resolution needs scene WORLD COORDINATES, which no extracted
      table carries - the 48-byte DATA00 scene record is name+h+cls+flag+link, fully
      consumed - so the placements must come from the per-map data or the FA.exe scene
      loader (Ghidra session). That is the v423f5+ track.

      FALSIFY: (a) a ground-start pilot parks -> grant within ~SETTLE+poll, log line
      'ground-stop at AF=..'; (b) a session containing a bail or respawn NEVER produces a
      grant while the plane is airborne; (c) a pilot who takes off and lands again IS
      granted (the old first-gate skip is gone); (d) a parked pilot on a lossy link gets
      exactly ONE grant per stop. REVERT: AUTO_RESUPPLY=False is the live kill-switch; full
      revert = restore this entry's diff.

      NEXT (v423f5+): explicit Arcade/TC policy split keyed on scoring_mode_for_room();
      position-based field attribution; decode the msg-73/0x49 SendRepairInfo REPLY (39B,
      FUN_004c8690) - if it carries the amounts actually drawn, debit real figures and
      delete the nominal SUPPLY_DEBIT_* constants.

