v419f5: [DIAGNOSTIC] STALL-WATCH REBUILT ON THE ONE CONDITION THAT CANNOT FALSE-FIRE - a
      send that has OUTLIVED its blocking window (RELKEEP active, s._relkeep_held > 0).
      THE FALSE-POSITIVE CLASS (Celt_20260809_025032 + run_20260808_204942): v323's pend>0
      counted sends still INSIDE their normal 5s blocking window at the scan instant, so an
      HQ-idle client - 622s with no reliable DATA to send, acks_in climbing the whole time
      (channel healthy; _rel_rx_time stamps DATA only, never ACKs), nothing flowing but the
      2.0s/36B 0x7d0 keepalive beacon - plus one transient in-window send produced a warn and
      a junk flightrec dump. 2733 dumps accumulated since Jul 6, most of them this shape.
      NEW TRIGGER: held>0 AND unreliable RX <3s AND not already warned. held>0 only happens
      after `to` (3-5s) of retransmits with no ACK - the exact failure the watcher exists
      for; a client with nothing to say can never trip it. rel_idle>=20 is DROPPED from the
      trigger (an ACK-path stall can coexist with flowing reliable DATA and still deserves a
      dump) and demoted to log-line context. Dead clients (no unreliable either) stay silent
      - the idle reaper owns them.
      TICK-VS-BEACON DISCRIMINATOR: s._tick_rx_time is stamped only when _rec_decode_telem
      identifies a real 0x42 object-update (the 96B incrementing-tick telemetry), never for
