      (tick 0.3s ago)' vs 'ALIVE-NO-TICKS (menu/load screen, beacon only)' - so a dump says
      at a glance whether the victim was flying (_Butterz_ 020823 shape) or stuck at a
      screen (the 82%-class victim is exactly ALIVE-NO-TICKS).
      RE-ARM: _rel_keeper maintains the held counter under s._lock (increment at takeover,
      decrement before rme on every exit path); when the LAST held send resolves by ACK on a
      session that had warned, _stall_warned/_rec_dumped re-arm and 'ACK flow RESTORED' logs
      - covering the client that recovers its ACKs without ever sending reliable DATA (the
      old re-arm only fired on DATA arrival).
      REPLAYED against the field cases: Celt suppressed, _Butterz_ seq=334 fires IN-FLIGHT,
      a synthetic 82%-victim fires ALIVE-NO-TICKS, a dead client stays silent.
      FALSIFY: flightrec dump rate collapses (baseline ~58 fires/session -> only genuine
      keeper-active stalls); every remaining warn coincides with a RELKEEP takeover on the
