v393f5: [CRITICAL/PROTOCOL] Complete the v392f5 LENGTH-RULE fix: the catalog escape must cover
      the WHOLE tb dispatch chain, not just 0x12. Field report (war date 21.05.1940 + fighters-
      only): GB hangar showed ONLY the Hurricane Mk.1 of its 3 eligible fighters; at 1941 GB
      recovered but USA showed NOTHING of its 4. Both are the same collision at other type
      values - NO client-side date logic involved (the missing Spitfire was arithmetic, not
      history):
        * GB@1940: 3 fighters -> catalog size 4 -> T=0x42 -> the tb==0x42 block's default is a
          VERBATIM echo of the flat 1-byte upload; the client's msg-58 decoder reads
          (Size-1)/3 = 1 record = the FIRST uploaded id = Hurr-Ia. One plane shown.
        * USA@1941: 4 fighters -> size 5 -> T=0x52 -> the tb==0x52 block's else is 'accepted
          (not echoed)' - a SWALLOW. Zero records, empty hangar. (The session log will show
          'type=0x52 sub=0x3a ... accepted (not echoed)'.)
        * GB@1941: 6 fighters -> size 7 -> T=0x72 -> no block -> correct re-encode ('more
          aircraft are listed').
      FULL COLLISION SURFACE (plane count n -> size n+1 -> T): n%16==0 -> 0x12 (fixed v392f5),
      n%16==1 -> 0x22 (verbatim: 1 plane owned, 0 shown), n%16==3 -> 0x42 (verbatim: first id
      only), n%16==4 -> 0x52 (swallow: none shown). 0x62/0x82/0x92 are sub-gated (0xe4/0xc8/
      0xdc) and immune; 0x01/0x00 can't match (catalog T low nibble is always 2).
      FIX: the v392f5 _catalog_3a escape now gates all four vulnerable blocks (0x12, 0x22,
      0x42, 0x52); an escaped catalog falls through to the single 0x3a re-encode handler, same
      as every non-colliding size always did. The re-encode replies via build_ingame_pkt (fresh
      type from RESPONSE size), so the 'never echo type=0x52' rule is not violated. Simulated
      the full matrix n=0..32: every colliding count now re-encodes correctly; pilot create/
      delete/rename (0xe2/0xe3/0xe7) and DisplayPilots/SetArena/gamedef/213 (0xe0/0xd7/0xd4/
      0xd5) still enter their blocks untouched.
      FALSIFY: (1) GB at 21.05.1940 shows Hurr-Ia + Spit-Ia + Martlet_I (3) and logs
      're-encoded 3'; (2) USA at 1941 shows F4F-3 + P-39D + P-40C + P-40E-1 (4), 're-encoded
      4'; (3) pilot create/delete/rename still work; (4) Display Pilots popup and arena list
      still work; (5) no 0x52 echo retry loops.
      REVERT: drop the three 'and not _catalog_3a' clauses (v392f5's 0x12 clause can stay).

v392f5: [CRITICAL/PROTOCOL] Empty GB hangar under the v391f5 fighters-only filter - a LENGTH-RULE
      collision, not a filter bug. Diagnosed from run_20260803_000702 + messages10: every side's
      0x3a catalog upload got its 'POST-AUTH re-encoded N (3-byte recs)' echo EXCEPT GB's, whose
      two attempts (00:10:02, 00:11:13) produced no echo and no CAREER push at all.
      ROOT CAUSE: the client's appspace type byte ENCODES THE PAYLOAD SIZE - T = ((size & 0xF)
      << 4) | 2, bc = size >> 4 (verified across all five captured sides: GB 17B->0x12,
      US 15B->0xf2, SU 13B->0xd2, GE 16B->0x02, JP 14B->0xe2). The handle_post_auth appspace
      dispatch keyed on `tb == 0x12` as if 0x12 were a fixed type marker, but any upload whose
      payload is exactly 16k+1 bytes arrives with T=0x12. A catalog of EXACTLY 16 plane ids
      (1 sub + 16 ids = 17 bytes) is precisely that shape - and fighters-only cut GB to exactly
      its 16 fighters. The block has no 0x3a case, so its catch-all return swallowed the
      request; the 3-byte re-echo (which IS the hangar pool since v384f5) never fired; and the
      client's retry re-sends the identical 17-byte payload, so the hangar stayed empty
      permanently. Pre-filter GB uploaded 28 planes (29B -> T=0xd2), which is why this never
      showed before; ANY side reaching a multiple of 16 planes (war-date, fighters-only, roster
      edits) would reproduce it. Likely the same class as the v337/v339 'lobby-phase blind
      spot' around msg 58.
      FIX: one guard - the appspace block's entry condition now excludes the catalog shape:
      `if tb == 0x12 and not _catalog_3a`, where _catalog_3a = direct sub==0x3a OR the prefixed
      form (sub==0x00 with pl[8]==0x3a; inside the block sub==0x00 was only ever consulted for
      pl[8]==0xd2/0x43, so the prefixed catalog was equally catch-all-swallowed - rescuing it
      changes nothing else). Excluded packets fall through to the existing 0x3a re-encode
      handler unchanged. Simulated against all five captured packets: GB now parses (size=17,
      16 ids) and echoes; US/SU/GE/JP dispatch identically to before; genuine appspace 0x12
      requests (0xe1 pilot list, 0xd2 arena list, 0x43 polls) still enter the block.
      FALSIFY: (1) GB hangar populates in the fighters-only arena and the T=0x12 request logs
      're-encoded 16'; (2) other sides unchanged; (3) arena list + pilot list + 0x43 polls
      still work (the block's real traffic); (4) no new 'unknown message' floods.
      REVERT: restore `if tb == 0x12:` (delete the _catalog_3a line and the `and not` clause).

