v380f5: [HANGAR] PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG = True -> False. Switches per-side hangar filtering from
      the 0x3a catalog echo (which never actually filtered the DISPLAY) to the native GAME_DEF
      byte-0 flyability gate. Addresses the 'other nations' planes bleed into every side' symptom.

      WHY (settled after the v375-v379 detour): the client draws each plane's nation TAB from the
      GAME_DEF plane-info array byte 0 (FUN_006de570; documented in the apply_plane_byte0_override
      docstring), NOT from the 0x3a echo. Under True, apply_plane_teams writes byte0=0x1f (all camps)
      for every plane, so the GAME_DEF says 'every plane belongs to every side' and the hangar shows
      the full all-nation list on every side - exactly the bleed. The 0x3a echo only ever controlled
      list MEMBERSHIP, never the nation-tab display, so it could not fix the bleed no matter what it
      sent. This was NOT an ordering bug: Me-163B is correctly hidden for a non-mod, which proves the
      byte0-override at slot 118 hit the right plane => the GAME_DEF plane block is in PLANE_ROSTER
      order, and all three orderings (PLANE_ROSTER, the 0x3a upload id-space, the GAME_DEF block)
      agree. (This is also why v378's Preload-order reorder was wrong and was reverted in v379.)

      FIX: False makes apply_plane_teams write byte0 = (1<<camp) per plane, so FUN_00438330 greys
      wrong-nation planes and each side's hangar shows only its own aircraft. Verified per slot:
      US=0x01 GB=0x02 SU=0x04 GE=0x08 JP=0x10, correctly assigned to Pe-8->SU, A6M2->JPN,
      Dauntless->GB, C-47A/SBD-2->USA, etc.

      SAFETY (the v332 bit-7 CTD): under False, camp 7 (NU) would make apply_plane_teams write
      1<<7 = 0x80, the UNTESTED byte-0 value that caused the v332 arena-page CTD (crashes the page
      for EVERYONE, not just the viewer). GUARDED: apply_plane_teams now writes 0x00 for any camp
      >= 5 (NU + unused 5/6) instead of 1<<camp. The NU planes (Me-163B, and the v377 movers
      Ouragan/Tunnan/HA-200) therefore get byte0=0x00 = flyable by no standard nation. Me-163B is
      then set to 0x80 by PLANE_BYTE0_OVERRIDE (the TESTED single-slot path, already live-verified
      as 'hidden for non-mod'); apply_plane_hide also zeroes staff planes. Confirmed NO plane
      receives 0x80 from the bulk apply_plane_teams loop.

      KNOWN LIMITATION / FOLLOW-UP: the three NON-Me-163B NU movers (Ouragan 113, Tunnan 112,
      HA-200 46) now get byte0=0x00 and have NO override, so under False they appear on NO nation
      tab - effectively hidden from everyone including NU admins. They were staff/NU-only anyway so
      this is not a regression from normal play, but if they should be flyable on the NU tab they
      need adding to PLANE_BYTE0_OVERRIDE ({..., 113:0x80, 112:0x80, 46:0x80}). NOT done here
      because 0x80-as-NU-tab is only proven for Me-163B via 'hidden', not via 'appears on NU' -
      verify the Me-163B actually shows on an admin's NU tab first, then extend the override.

      THE OPEN RISK (why this is a live test, not a settled fix): True was originally chosen because
      the byte0 gate shrinks the per-side flyable list on a side change, which historically forced a
      heavy leave/re-entry handshake that HUNG the HQ menu. The reliability work since (v371 256-
      wedge cure, universal counter-unwrap, event-driven queue drain) targets exactly that wedge, so
      the hang may no longer occur - but this is UNVERIFIED. FALSIFY: (1) each side's hangar shows
      ONLY its own nation's planes (bleed gone); (2) switching sides at the team-select/HQ screen
      does NOT freeze the menu. If (2) fails, flip PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG back to True (one flag)
      and the bleed returns but side-switching is smooth - then the fix is to repair the side-change
      handshake rather than the filter path.

