v378f5: [IDENTITY/CRITICAL] PLANE_ROSTER RE-ALIGNED TO THE CLIENT'S PLANE-ID SPACE. This is the
      true root cause behind the ENTIRE multi-session hangar saga (v375-v377): the wrong-flag
      planes, the nation moves "not working", and the mislabeled hangars. It was never the filter
      and never the per-plane teams.

      GROUND TRUTH (client-side log messages85.log): the client's 'Preload available planes' list
      IS the client's internal aircraft order - i.e. THE plane-id namespace that every 0x3a catalog
      byte, spawn ONumber, and kill/telemetry record is expressed in. Comparing it to the server's
      PLANE_ROSTER: SAME 121 names, but the ORDER disagreed at 110 of 121 positions. So the server
      was speaking a different plane-id dialect than the client: it filtered/echoed the catalog
      using ITS ids, the client rendered them using ITS ids, and every position where the two
      diverged showed the wrong aircraft. Concretely, that produced EXACTLY the reported symptoms:
        - USA hangar showed Dauntless + Dakota (GB variants); GB was missing both.
        - GB showed Pe-8 + Li-2 (SU); SU showed Ju-88 + Ju-52 (GE); GE showed HA-200 + D3A.
        - JPN showed SBD-2 + C-47A (USA) and was MISSING the A6M2.
      All of it is one bug: a scrambled id<->name table.

      FIX: PLANE_ROSTER re-ordered to EXACTLY equal the client Preload order (verified list ==
      client order, 121 planes, same set). Because EVERY other plane attribute - PLANE_VALUE_2004,
      PLANE_VALUE_NAMES, BOMBER_PLANE_NAMES, PLANE_TEAMS, STAFF_ONLY_PLANES - is keyed BY NAME, they
      all follow the reorder automatically; PLANE_ROSTER is the ONLY positional (index-keyed) table.
      Two hardcoded id-literals were updated to match the new order:
        - PLANE_BYTE0_OVERRIDE: Me-163B 118 -> 65 (its client-preload id).
        - the L2D2 "client omits id 107" comment -> id 120 (L2D2's new id). (STAFF_ONLY_PLANE_IDS is
          computed by name via enumerate(PLANE_ROSTER), so it needed no change.)

      VERIFIED before deploy (simulated the real 0x3a upload against the new roster + PLANE_TEAMS):
        - all 13 of the user's specific complaints resolve: USA loses Dauntless/Dakota, GB gains
          both and loses Pe-8/Li-2, SU loses Ju-88/Ju-52, GE loses HA-200/D3A, JPN loses SBD-2/
          C-47A and REGAINS the A6M2.
        - per-side kept counts (real catalog): USA 24, GB 28, SU 21, GE 23, JPN 19.
        - value/class spot-check by new id: F4U-4C(id13)=2000, A6M2(id68)=1150 fighter, SBD-2(id80)
          =650 bomber, Pe-8(id97)=1150 bomber - all correct; 4 newsletter anchors still exact;
          bomber count still 41.
      Compiles clean; on-disk byte-identical to the tested replica.

      IMPORTANT GOING FORWARD: PLANE_ROSTER is now INDEX-LOCKED to the client. Do NOT reorder it
      without a fresh client Preload capture. If a future client build adds/reorders planes, re-pull
      the Preload list and re-align. The old (pre-v378) order should be considered CORRUPT - any
