v377f5: [HANGAR/ECONOMY-DATA + CLEANUP] Nation moves + close-out of the v375/v376 diagnostic
      detour. THREE parts:

      (1) THE FILTER WAS NEVER BROKEN - RESOLVED. The v375/v376 hunt for a "dead" side-catalog
      filter was chasing a LOGGING artifact, not a code fault. Proof chain:
        * v376f5's CATDIAG2 fired with guard1=True, guard2=True, kept=25 (USA) / 29 (GB) on real
          hangar opens (run_20260730_082408, _083652) - the filter enters, computes, and reaches
          the send. build_ingame_pkt is a 3-line byte-packer that cannot raise on that input, and
          the send_reply thread is spawned right after.
        * The reason NO run ever showed the 'catalog filtered' confirmation: fa_logging._TAG_LEVELS
          maps 'POST-AUTH' -> DEBUG, and the file log level defaults to INFO
          (FILE_LOG_LEVEL_DEFAULT='INFO'). Every POST-AUTH line, including the filter confirmation,
          is DEBUG and is filtered out of run_*.log. It was NEVER muted - 'logunmute POST-AUTH' had
          no effect because mute and level are independent gates. CATDIAG/CATDIAG2 aren't in
          _TAG_LEVELS so they default to INFO and showed, which is the ONLY reason they were
          visible while POST-AUTH wasn't.
        LESSON: 'grep TAG = 0 hits' does not mean the code path is untaken if TAG is DEBUG and the
        file is at INFO. Check the tag's level before concluding a feature is dead. The earlier
        'the filter has never fired' claim was wrong on exactly this point.

      FIX for visibility: the filter-confirmation line is now emitted with level='INFO' (the tag
      stays POST-AUTH; only that one call is lifted) so the proof-of-fire line shows at the normal
      file level from now on. To see the full DEBUG firehose for a repro, still use `loglevel file
      DEBUG` and set it back after (DEBUG ~= 55MB / 8-player session).

      Removed the v375 CATDIAG block and the two v376 CATDIAG2 lines - they served their purpose.
      The filter body is back to its pre-diagnostic form (behaviour unchanged; verified the block
      is byte-clean of CATDIAG).

      (2) NATION MOVES (PLANE_TEAMS). Now safe to apply because the per-side filter is confirmed
      working - a moved plane actually shows on its new side's hangar:
        * Dauntless (id 60)  USA(default) -> GB (camp 1). The FAA Fleet Air Arm Dauntless. This is
          a SEPARATE roster entry from the US Navy "SBD-2" (id 104), which STAYS USA. (The user's
          earlier "SBD-2 -> US" note was the same display confusion; SBD-2 was already USA.)
        * Ouragan (id 113)   GB -> NU (camp 7). French Dassault MD.450 - post-war, not a WWII
          Allied type.
        * Tunnan  (id 112)   GB -> NU (camp 7). Swedish SAAB J29.
        * HA-200  (id 46)    GE -> NU (camp 7). Spanish Hispano HA-200 Saeta - post-war, not Axis.
      NOTE: NU (camp 7) is the ADMIN-ONLY side, so Ouragan/Tunnan/HA-200 are now STAFF-VISIBLE
      ONLY (same gating as the Me-163B), not flyable by everyone. That is the correct reading of
      "move to NEU"; if any of them should instead be world-flyable, they need a real national
      side, not NU. Per-side kept counts after the move (on the real client catalog): USA 24, GB
