v375f5: [DIAG/HANGAR] Instrumentation for the SIDE-CATALOG FILTER, which a catalog capture proved
      has NEVER fired. Investigating the reported "wrong flag" planes (Pe-8/Li-2 shown GB, Ju-88/
      Ju-52 shown SU, A6M2/L2D2 shown GE) led to a bigger finding than a per-plane teams error:

      GROUND TRUTH (run_20260730_074736, Bigalon's 0x3a upload decoded):
        * The client's catalog is a fixed 119-id DISPLAY-ORDER list (it omits id 107 L2D2 and id
          118 Me-163B). Our PLANE_ROSTER maps every id->name CORRECTLY against it - the roster is
          NOT shifted, so the earlier off-by-one theory is disproved.
        * Simulating the server's own side-filter on that real upload yields PERFECT national
          groupings (USA 25, GB 29, SU 22, GE 25, JPN 18) - Pe-8->SU, Ju-88->GE, A6M2->JPN all
          correct. So when the filter FIRES, the hangar is right.
        * But `catalog filtered` appears in ZERO runs (every log checked). The per-side filter has
          never once executed, so the client always falls back to its OWN built-in nation grouping
          - which is the wrong-flag source. This is a WHOLE-FEATURE outage, not six mislabeled
          planes.

      Static analysis narrowed it to the filter's outer guard evaluating False at runtime even
      though sub==0x3a, PLANE_FILTER_VIA_CATALOG==True, and the pilot is on a side: the remaining
      suspect is s.nation being None when the QUEUED 0x3a is drained (handle_post_auth runs off the
      post_auth_cmds queue, so it can process the catalog after a later 'LEFT team' reset nation to
      None). The CAREER block (same function, needs only entered_game) fires; the filter (needs
      _have_side) does not - consistent with nation==None at filter time.

      THIS VERSION adds a CATDIAG log on every 0x3a that reaches the filter, dumping sub, _cat_pfx,
      the filter flag, s.nation, _have_side, _hide count, and entered_game. Diagnostic only - no
      behaviour change, one log line. Next hangar-open session will show exactly which gate is
      False, then the real fix follows (likely: resolve the catalog against the side the client is
      actually browsing rather than s.nation, or re-run the filter when nation is set).
      FALSIFY/READ: open the hangar on a side; expect a CATDIAG line. If it shows nation=None while
      the pilot is on a side, the queue-ordering hypothesis is confirmed.

      NOTE on the requested NATION MOVES (Dauntless->GB, Ouragan/Tunnan/HA-200->NEU): deliberately
      NOT applied yet. They are PLANE_TEAMS edits that only take visible effect once the filter
      actually fires, so they are held until v375f5's diagnosis lands the filter fix - otherwise
      they would be invisible and untestable.

