v373f5: [IDENTITY/CRITICAL] *** UNTESTED IN LIVE PLAY AS OF THIS BASELINE - fix deployed and
      compile-verified, but the falsification run below has NOT yet been observed. *** RECYCLED-SLOT
      MISATTRIBUTION - a departed player's telemetry straggler
      resurrected his identity on peers. Reported against v371f5: "Taurus shot and hit ALL41_MAD
      but Taurus's client showed him as AC2E_Bigalon, who had been out of the game for minutes."

      TRACE (run_20260729_210316 + messages08, room 53):
        21:03:55  AC2E_Bigalon -> ClientNumber=0 PlayerIndex=0 (holds PI 0 all session)
        21:34:33  Bigalon presses back-to-lobby (msg 64). handle_leave_arena sends his DELETE3 +
                  msg-63 REMOVE and clears _created_peers. entered_game -> False.
        21:34:33.694  <-- THE BUG: a telemetry datagram of Bigalon's, already in flight before the
                  leave, reaches relay_telemetry ~400ms later. Nothing there checked that the SOURCE
                  had left, so the lazy-create block saw an empty _created_peers and RE-CREATED his
                  object+player on ALL41_MAD ('create-object(object-only) AC2E_Bigalon -> ALL41_MAD').
                  That re-bound PlayerIndex 0 to Bigalon on the peers, undoing the REMOVE.
        21:35:35  ALL41_MAD recycles into the freed slot -> ClientNumber=0 PlayerIndex=0.
                  Taurus still had PI 0 bound to the resurrected Bigalon -> renders/attributes
                  ALL41_MAD's plane and hits as AC2E_Bigalon.

      This is the same misattribution FAMILY as the v348/v353/v355 teardown fixes, but every one of
      those closed a hole on the LEAVING/RE-JOINING path (make sure peers are TOLD to drop the
      departing player). The leak this time was on the SENDER's TELEMETRY path: even with a correct
      teardown, a single straggling flight datagram processed after the leave re-created the player
