      First INTERNET field deployment (v362f5, 6 players) turned the counter/TIME-attach
      wrapper from an occasional LAN quirk into a constant: internet jitter makes clients
      resync time continuously, so a large fraction of ALL datagrams arrive wrapped
      ([00][ctr][00][00] | inner). Every field report maps to a swallowed wrap:
        * GHOSTS (Gary, Warrior): 14 wrapped DELETE 0x03 hit the capture catch-all -
          one single swallowed message carried FOUR object deletes (0x0109/0x0119/
          0x011d/0x0117). Dead planes never removed from peers.
        * HITS NOT REGISTERING (Warrior, Moira, Taurus 4-hits-counted-as-1): 16
          wrapped DAMAGE28 0x1c never reached the damage relay.
        * NO PLANES / NO ARENAS (Moira, Taurus x2, Gary, MAD): wrapped catalog/list
          requests swallowed; plus wrapped room-polls 0x43 (14x), team-selects 0x44
          (36x), ExitEvents 0x21, reassigns 0x0e, map/supply 0x40/0x53/0x54.
        * DISPATCH TRACEBACK 23:28:15.713 (struct.error, buffer size 5): wrapped
          CANOPY telemetry false-matched relay_telemetry's offset-0 scan (ctr low
          nibble 0x2 + inner bc 0x07 = a TELEM_OPCODE), shadowing the correct
          offset-4 match; v341 truncated 126B to a 5B stub off the wrapper's fake
          declaration and the re-stamp crashed on it. For other counters the stub
          is >=7B: garbage got tick-stamped and RELAYED while the real frame died.
      The per-message scan handlers accumulated since v327 (chat), v352 (damage
      prefix), v358 (0xd2), v363 (para out-4) were whack-a-mole against a universal
      phenomenon. THREE EDITS:
      (1) handle_post_auth: GENERIC unwrap beside the _pfx reframe - cmd==0,
          pl[0]==0, inner header well-formed (pl[6:8]==0000), EXACT arithmetic
          8+pl[4]*16+(pl[5]>>4)==len(pl), and direct interpretation WINS ties (a
          real 19B para out-4 is never mistaken for a wrap). REPLACES/SUBSUMES the
          v363f5 parachute-only block. Validated against all 25 distinct wrapped
          payload shapes in the field log: 25/25 unwrap; every known direct form
          untouched. Logs 'REFRAME ... counter-wrap ctr=... -> stripped' per unwrap
          (deliberately chatty for the first field runs; demote later if noisy).
