v348: [SESSION/CRITICAL] a session that ended WITHOUT msg 64 never told in-game peers, so the
      recycled ClientNumber/PlayerIndex was inherited by the next joiner while peers still had
      the departed pilot bound to it. Misattributed hits, kills and collisions.

      SYMPTOM (reported): "Moira had left the game, Cheech shot me up and collided, but my
      screen and chat log show Moira@HQ scored the hits and collision."

      ROOT CAUSE: only the msg-64 back-to-lobby path sent the in-game teardown (v182/v191:
      type-3 object DELETE then msg-63 CP_OP_REMOVE). Every other way a session ends - client
      crash, socket reset, reap-on-reconnect, timeout - did only
          broadcast_player_leave()   (LOBBY UI list only)
          broadcast_system(); db_room_leave()
          _free_start_place(); free_client_number()   <- slot straight back in the pool
      No object delete, no player removal. The slot was then handed to the next joiner while
      every peer still mapped it to the previous pilot and still had their ghost plane.
      TIMELINE (run_20260726_090535_1_, room 53):
        17:57:58 Moira@HQ -> ClientNumber=0 PlayerIndex=0
        18:00:30 Moira spawns ONumber=0x0100, peers told
        18:01:0x Moira's session ends - NO LEAVE, NO REAP, NO DELETE3, NO msg-63 REMOVE
        18:01:28 Taurus sends a delete for 0x0100 (Moira's ghost) -> server no longer knows the
                 object -> "neither its own nor any peer's" -> swallowed. THIS LINE IS THE PROOF
                 OF DIVERGENCE: the peer was trying to clean up something the server had already
                 forgotten, three minutes before the collision.
        18:01:30 Cheech -> ClientNumber=0 PlayerIndex=0   <- Moira's recycled slot
        18:04:5x Cheech (obj 0x0113) damages and collides with Taurus -> reported as Moira@HQ
      Client-side corroboration: "Add existing REMOTE_PLAYER" and the
      "AceOrRankChangedCB. PlayerIndex=N not found" floods - which is also the long-standing
      ACE88 mystery, now explained rather than merely observed.

      FIX: teardown_ingame_presence(s, why) - the same DELETE-then-REMOVE the msg-64 path sends,
      preserving the v191 ordering (plane before player, or a flying peer use-after-frees the
      dangling NetPlane). Called from the reap path BEFORE free_client_number returns the slot.
      Guarded on entered_game and wrapped in try/except so a teardown failure cannot break
      session cleanup. New log tag: [TEARDOWN].

      NOT ADMIN-RELATED: rights were only ever granted to Moira@HQ, AC2E_Bigalon, Taurus@FA and
      Sparky@FA. _AvA_Insane was NEVER an admin and hit the same class of failure.

      UNCONFIRMED: Moira's session produced no REAP line at all, so it may have ended by a path
      other than the reap cleanup. If [TEARDOWN] does not appear on a hard disconnect, the same
      call has to be added wherever that path lives.

