v339: [RESUPPLY] REVERTED v338's engine-OFF re-park. Removes the mid-air re-park risk;
      the root bug is deliberately left OPEN rather than papered over.

      v338 restored at_airfield from _last_af on engine-off, on the theory that engine-off
      means the pilot has landed. That conflates two different things and is wrong in BOTH
      directions:
        * AIR START, no takeoff -> there is no launch field, so _last_af is None and the
          restore did nothing; resupply still never fired for those pilots.
        * ENGINE CUT IN THE AIR (glide, stall, battle damage) -> it re-parked the plane at a
          field it may be nowhere near, potentially setting at_airfield WHILE AIRBORNE. Firing
          a msg-60 rearm mid-flight is exactly what v277 exists to prevent - it rebuilds the
          plane object and FREEZES the client. The settle/freshness guards make that unlikely,
          not impossible, and 'engine off and looks static' is a far weaker guarantee than
          'parked at a field'.

      ROOT BUG STILL OPEN: at_airfield is only ever SET from StartPlace (spawn) and CLEARED on
      engine-on (takeoff), with nothing to restore it after a landing - so _resupply_poll_loop's
      first gate rejects any plane that took off and came back.
      THE CORRECT FIX is to resolve the field FROM POSITION on engine-off. fa_scenes.json
      carries 722 scenes across 14 terrains, so a nearest-field + altitude check handles the
      air-start case AND correctly resolves to nothing for a mid-air engine cut. Do that rather
      than reaching for _last_af again.

